  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Assessing Core Capabilities**\n\nI\'m considering the comprehensive Vulnerability Intelligence platform, encompassing ingestion, matching, classification, and remediation. I\'m focusing on its enterprise-grade nature and how it aligns with critical standards and tracking capabilities. The platform includes a Security Operations component as well. I am now beginning an assessment of core skills.\n\n\n**Inspecting Required Features**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the concrete features to implement. The specification focuses on enterprise-grade, multi-source feed ingestion. I am setting aside unrelated components like cloud SQL, Firebase, and the Gemini API, ensuring the core functionality meets the enterprise-grade multi-source requirements, while considering in-memory, SQLite or JSON persistence with a REST API, and a robust pipeline simulator. My current focus is a clean, dark/light cybersecurity SOC interface.\n\n\n**Defining Feed Integrations**\n\nI\'m now integrating external vulnerability data from sources like NVD, CISA KEV, and others into a unified format. My focus is on robust threat feed management, including custom RSS, STIX, and JSON API sources with configurable authentication and rate limiting. I\'m prioritizing 16 pre-seeded vendor feeds and incorporating connectivity testing, health monitoring, and toggle functionalities. I am also planning CPE-first watch-list matching, exposure classification, and timeline scope filtering. Finally, I\'m working to deduplicate canonical CVEs.\n\n\n**Refining Alert Logic**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the alert logic. I\'ve standardized CVE IDs for efficient lookups. Auto-enrichment now populates missing data like CVSS scores and CPEs. My priority classification incorporates CISA KEV and EPSS scores, alongside CVSS thresholds. I\'m also generating remediation steps and tracking SLAs based on severity and source, including breach countdowns. Finally, I am updating the Web Application Views.\n\n\n**Detailing Key Outputs**\n\nI am now focusing on the outputs of the vulnerability platform. I\'m prioritizing asset management with exposure classification, and CPE tooling like a validator and generator, along with bulk JSON import/export. I am also working on the findings triage, filtering by various criteria and implementing a status workflow with remediation details. Furthermore, I am inspecting normalized threat intelligence, reviewing advisories, and the pipeline execution flow. Finally, I am tracking alerted CVEs and generating comprehensive reports.\n\n\n**Expanding Notification System**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the notification delivery system, tracking email history including provider statuses and logs. I\'m focusing on the threat feed management capabilities, including connectivity testing, health stats, and comprehensive source integration and customization. I\'m also addressing recipient management with email validation and subscription tiers, and designing an editable advisory template with live preview and test capabilities. I\'m also now focusing on system settings, operational logs, and system health status. Finally, I am implementing user profile and security features, including password policies.\n\n\n"
