  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Styling Choices**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing `src/index.css`. The presence of `@import \"tailwindcss\";` suggests a strong styling foundation. Now, I\'m focusing on enhancements for a polished cybersecurity console. My priorities are to optimize typography, fine-tune font families, implement dark background styling, and customize scrollbars. The goal is a top-tier, crisp aesthetic.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the core data structures needed for the console, starting with `NormalizedCVE` in `src/types/index.ts`. This involves specifying all the fields, like `cveId`, `title`, `description`, and the associated metadata, including CVSS scores, CWEs, CPE matches, and the source feeds to consume. I am also working on how to track CISA KEV data, EPSS data, and the exploit status of each vulnerability.\n\n\n**Constructing Data Models**\n\nI\'m now deep in defining crucial data models. Specifically, I am fleshing out the `remediation` structure, detailing patch URLs, immediate actions, workarounds, rollback plans, step-by-step instructions, and vendor advisory references. I\'m also creating `WatchListItem` with details like vendor, product, CPEs, exposure levels, and the like. Finally, I\'m working on the `Finding` structure to connect CVEs to assets, define priorities, and establish SLAs.\n\n\n**Detailing State Transitions**\n\nI\'m now detailing the state transition aspects of findings and integrating threat feed configurations. I\'m focusing on defining properties like `slaBreached`, `slaTimeRemainingMinutes`, and the various status options. I\'m also including `alertedAt`, `reAlertCount`, and `advisoryId`. I\'m working on the `timelineEvents` array to track the history. Finally, I\'m working on the `ThreatFeed` and `Advisory` structures. I\'m thinking about including `healthStatus`, `lastSync`, `latencyMs` and other fields for operational insights.\n\n\n**Defining Alert Metrics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the data structure for alerts, starting with fields such as `title`, `severity`, `cveIds`, and associated `findings`. I\'m also considering `createdDate`, `deliveryStatus`, `recipientCount`, and how to include an `executiveSummary` and remediation instructions. I am also working on `affectedSystems` and, in more detail, a `PipelineExecution` structure. This includes tracking timestamps, statuses, scope, phases and stats.\n\n\n**Structuring Alert Delivery**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the alert delivery mechanism data structure. I\'m deep diving into the `AlertedCVE` interface, focusing on tracking statuses such as `ACTIVE_REMEDIATION`, `RESOLVED`, and `SUPPRESSED`. I\'m also including `recipientEmails`, `reAlertReason`, and the `advisoriesDispatched` count. I am also planning the `EmailRecipient` with attributes like `subscriptionTier` and `deliverySuccessRate`, and the `EmailLog` structure.\n\n\n**Defining Configuration Structures**\n\nI\'m now outlining the application settings data structure. I\'m focusing on attributes like the general `timestamp` and `category` levels. I\'m also thinking about `AppSettings`, and its parameters such as `scopeHours`, `schedulerIntervalMinutes`, and `advisoryPrefix`. Furthermore, I\'m working on `mailgunConfig` and `smtpConfig` to configure email. I am also planning `ssrfProtection` and `securityPolicy` settings. I\'m currently defining `ntpConfig` and `slaTiers`.\n\n\n**Enumerating SLAs and Feeds**\n\nI\'m working on the `SLATiers` configuration, defining time-based metrics and alert escalation policies. Now I\'m shifting focus to pre-seeded feeds, specifically `src/data/seedData.ts`. I\'m documenting the 16 vendor feeds, including Microsoft, Fortinet, Cisco, and others. The idea is to cover key attack surfaces.\n\n\n**Cataloging Vulnerabilities**\n\nI am now focusing on populating the console with real-world vulnerabilities, like CVE-2024-38077 and others. My attention is on capturing critical details. This includes precise CPE 2.3 expressions, CVSS v3.1 vector strings and scores, and associated CWE codes. I am also gathering EPSS scores, CISA KEV dates, required actions, and ransomware tags to enhance the console\'s effectiveness. Finally, I\'m integrating remediation playbooks with patch links and mitigation steps.\n\n\n**Refining Matcher Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the logic within `src/engine/`. I\'ve been working on refining the CPE 2.3 parser in `cpeMatcher.ts` and improving wildcard support for more flexible matching. I\'m also ensuring a robust CVE normalizer in `deduplicator.ts` for efficient lookups. Finally, I\'m integrating data enrichment within `enrichmentEngine.ts` to seamlessly merge data.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Pipeline Execution**\n\nI\'m deep in the implementation of `pipelineRunner.ts`. I am meticulously constructing the autonomous pipeline orchestrator and focusing on the seven distinct phases: Ingestion, Deduplication & Normalization, Auto-Enrichment, Watch-List Matching, Priority Classification & SLA Assignment, Remediation Playbook Generation, and Advisory Report Persistence & Delivery. My focus is on robust execution with latency and SSRF checks, efficient data structures, and actionable outputs.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard Features**\n\nI\'m now designing the user interface, especially the dashboard. I\'m focusing on key performance indicators (KPI) like monitored assets and findings. I\'m thinking about an \"Exposure Radar\" visualization, severity distribution charts, and an SLA countdown urgency board. I\'m also planning a pipeline execution log for operational oversight. Furthermore, I\'m working on active feed health, and CSRF token and NTP status indicators.\n\n\n**Developing Advisory Exports**\n\nI\'m now focused on generating advisories. I\'m excited about including a full Advisory Viewer with instant PDF export and download options, along with Copy Markdown/HTML. I\'m also including a unified normalized CVE table with data from NVD, OpenCVE, GHSA, VulCheck, and EPSS, plus the CISA KEV badge. Also, I\'m working on raw JSON inspectors.\n\n\n**Implementing Alert Delivery**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the alert generation and distribution mechanism. I\'m structuring recipient lists, assigning roles and tiers, and tracking delivery success. I\'m also planning the advisory template, a live visual editor with variable tokens and preview capabilities for desktop and mobile clients. I\'m integrating email delivery logs with retry queues and bounce status visualization. I am also working on operational logs for auditing and system health checks, including SSRF protection and CSRF token monitoring. Furthermore, I\'m working on configurable scope hours and scheduler intervals.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_52351"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Configure styling with Tailwind font families and custom dark theme scrollbars\",\"EndLine\":2,\"Instruction\":\"Add base styling and font classes\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"@import \\\"tailwindcss\\\";\\n\\n@layer base {\\n  body {\\n    font-family: \'Plus Jakarta Sans\', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", Roboto, sans-serif;\\n    background-color: #0b0f17;\\n    color: #e2e8f0;\\n    overflow-x: hidden;\\n  }\\n\\n  code, pre, .font-mono {\\n    font-family: \'JetBrains Mono\', monospace;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/* Custom dark scrollbars */\\n::-webkit-scrollbar {\\n  width: 6px;\\n  height: 6px;\\n}\\n::-webkit-scrollbar-track {\\n  background: #0f172a;\\n}\\n::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {\\n  background: #334155;\\n  border-radius: 3px;\\n}\\n::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {\\n  background: #475569;\\n}\",\"StartLine\":1,\"TargetContent\":\"@import \\\"tailwindcss\\\";\",\"TargetFile\":\"/src/index.css\",\"toolAction\":\"Updating src/index.css\",\"toolSummary\":\"Configure base styles and dark theme scrollbars\"}"
