  planner_response {
    response: "### VulnStream Enterprise \342\200\224 Vulnerability Intelligence & Ingestion Platform\n\nA modern, enterprise-grade threat feed ingestion, CPE-first watch-list correlation, and autonomous SLA tracking platform designed for SOC and incident response teams.\n\n---\n\n### Core Architectural Features Built\n\n1. **Multi-Source Threat Feed Ingestion & SSRF Protection**\n   - **Unified Record Normalization**: Merges NVD CVE 2.0, OpenCVE, CISA KEV, GitHub Advisory Database (GHSA), OSV, VulCheck, and FIRST.org EPSS enrichment into a single canonical record format.\n   - **16 Pre-Seeded Vendor Feeds**: Microsoft MSRC, Fortinet PSIRT, Cisco Security, VMware/Broadcom STIX 2.1, Adobe, Palo Alto Networks Unit 42, Red Hat RHSA, Apple, Apache, Google Chrome, F5 Networks, Juniper Networks, Linux Kernel, Atlassian, Oracle CPU, and Citrix PSIRT.\n   - **SSRF Hardening**: Validates feed URLs against private networks (RFC 1918 `10.x`, `192.168.x`, `172.16-31.x`), loopbacks (`127.x`, `localhost`), link-local addresses, and blocks embedded credentials or unsafe redirects.\n   - **Credential Encryption**: API keys stored with PBKDF2 hash encryption at rest.\n\n2. **CPE-First Watch-List Matching & Asset Inventory**\n   - **Strict NIST IR 7695 CPE 2.3 Component Matching**: Compares `part`, `vendor`, `product`, and `version` with wildcard (`*`) and not-applicable (`-`) resolution, backed by vendor/product heuristic fallback.\n   - **Exposure Classification & Tier Escalation**: Supports `INTERNET_FACING` (perimeter), `INTERNAL_CRITICAL` (Active Directory, ESXi hypervisors), `DMZ`, `WORKSTATION`, and `CLOUD_INFRA`. Matching internet-facing assets automatically escalates priority by +1 tier (e.g., P2 $\\rightarrow$ P1, P1 $\\rightarrow$ P0).\n   - **Bulk JSON Import & Export**: Supports bulk JSON uploads of up to 1,000 asset records with schema validation and pre-populated samples.\n\n3. **Deduplication & Timeline Scope Window**\n   - **Canonical CVE Normalization**: Enforces canonical uppercase `CVE-YYYY-NNNN+` format.\n   - **$O(1)$ Deduplication**: Drops in-run duplicate records and cross-checks previously-alerted suppression registries.\n   - **Timeline Scope**: Configurable `scope_hours` (default 24h) checking published and modified timestamps against the active window.\n\n4. **Priority Classification & Dynamic SLA Tracking**\n   - **Tier Logic**:\n     - **P0 CISA KEV**: Mandatory 6-hour remediation SLA deadline.\n     - **P1 Critical**: CVSS $\\ge$ 9.0 or high EPSS ($>0.40$) with active weaponization (24h SLA).\n     - **P2 High**: CVSS $\\ge$ 7.0 (72h SLA).\n     - **P3 Medium**: CVSS $\\ge$ 4.0 (168h / 7d SLA).\n   - **SLA Countdown & Clock Resets**: Live ticking countdown with breach warnings, auto-escalation banners, and clock resets on tier promotion or re-alerting.\n\n5. **Remediation Playbook Generation**\n   - Per-CVE vendor advisory URLs, immediate containment actions, workarounds, rollback procedures, and step-by-step CLI commands with one-click copy.\n\n6. **Notification Delivery & Advisory Sandbox**\n   - **Security Advisories**: Complete advisory management (`ADV-2026-XXXX`) with delivery status and **one-click high-fidelity PDF export / print formatting**.\n   - **Live Advisory Template Sandbox**: Editable HTML email template with token replacement (`{{advisory_id}}`, `{{sla_hours}}`, `{{remediation_steps}}`) and test-dispatch modal.\n   - **Email History & Backoff Queue**: Exponential retry tracking (`5m` $\\rightarrow$ `15m` $\\rightarrow$ `1h` $\\rightarrow$ `3h` $\\rightarrow$ `12h`) with manual retry capability.\n   - **Recipient Management**: Distribution lists with email regex validation and subscription filters.\n\n7. **SOC Operations, Auditability & Health Telemetry**\n   - **Searchable Audit Trail**: Categorized audit logs (PIPELINE, SECURITY, FEED, WATCHLIST, AUTH, EMAIL) with CSV/JSON export.\n   - **Health Probes**: Dedicated `/live`, `/health`, and `/ready` status telemetry, Gunicorn multi-worker topology, NTP time drift monitoring, and security headers breakdown (CSP, X-Frame-Options DENY, HSTS, CSRF token validation, 30-min session timeout)."
    modified_response: "### VulnStream Enterprise \342\200\224 Vulnerability Intelligence & Ingestion Platform\n\nA modern, enterprise-grade threat feed ingestion, CPE-first watch-list correlation, and autonomous SLA tracking platform designed for SOC and incident response teams.\n\n---\n\n### Core Architectural Features Built\n\n1. **Multi-Source Threat Feed Ingestion & SSRF Protection**\n   - **Unified Record Normalization**: Merges NVD CVE 2.0, OpenCVE, CISA KEV, GitHub Advisory Database (GHSA), OSV, VulCheck, and FIRST.org EPSS enrichment into a single canonical record format.\n   - **16 Pre-Seeded Vendor Feeds**: Microsoft MSRC, Fortinet PSIRT, Cisco Security, VMware/Broadcom STIX 2.1, Adobe, Palo Alto Networks Unit 42, Red Hat RHSA, Apple, Apache, Google Chrome, F5 Networks, Juniper Networks, Linux Kernel, Atlassian, Oracle CPU, and Citrix PSIRT.\n   - **SSRF Hardening**: Validates feed URLs against private networks (RFC 1918 `10.x`, `192.168.x`, `172.16-31.x`), loopbacks (`127.x`, `localhost`), link-local addresses, and blocks embedded credentials or unsafe redirects.\n   - **Credential Encryption**: API keys stored with PBKDF2 hash encryption at rest.\n\n2. **CPE-First Watch-List Matching & Asset Inventory**\n   - **Strict NIST IR 7695 CPE 2.3 Component Matching**: Compares `part`, `vendor`, `product`, and `version` with wildcard (`*`) and not-applicable (`-`) resolution, backed by vendor/product heuristic fallback.\n   - **Exposure Classification & Tier Escalation**: Supports `INTERNET_FACING` (perimeter), `INTERNAL_CRITICAL` (Active Directory, ESXi hypervisors), `DMZ`, `WORKSTATION`, and `CLOUD_INFRA`. Matching internet-facing assets automatically escalates priority by +1 tier (e.g., P2 $\\rightarrow$ P1, P1 $\\rightarrow$ P0).\n   - **Bulk JSON Import & Export**: Supports bulk JSON uploads of up to 1,000 asset records with schema validation and pre-populated samples.\n\n3. **Deduplication & Timeline Scope Window**\n   - **Canonical CVE Normalization**: Enforces canonical uppercase `CVE-YYYY-NNNN+` format.\n   - **$O(1)$ Deduplication**: Drops in-run duplicate records and cross-checks previously-alerted suppression registries.\n   - **Timeline Scope**: Configurable `scope_hours` (default 24h) checking published and modified timestamps against the active window.\n\n4. **Priority Classification & Dynamic SLA Tracking**\n   - **Tier Logic**:\n     - **P0 CISA KEV**: Mandatory 6-hour remediation SLA deadline.\n     - **P1 Critical**: CVSS $\\ge$ 9.0 or high EPSS ($>0.40$) with active weaponization (24h SLA).\n     - **P2 High**: CVSS $\\ge$ 7.0 (72h SLA).\n     - **P3 Medium**: CVSS $\\ge$ 4.0 (168h / 7d SLA).\n   - **SLA Countdown & Clock Resets**: Live ticking countdown with breach warnings, auto-escalation banners, and clock resets on tier promotion or re-alerting.\n\n5. **Remediation Playbook Generation**\n   - Per-CVE vendor advisory URLs, immediate containment actions, workarounds, rollback procedures, and step-by-step CLI commands with one-click copy.\n\n6. **Notification Delivery & Advisory Sandbox**\n   - **Security Advisories**: Complete advisory management (`ADV-2026-XXXX`) with delivery status and **one-click high-fidelity PDF export / print formatting**.\n   - **Live Advisory Template Sandbox**: Editable HTML email template with token replacement (`{{advisory_id}}`, `{{sla_hours}}`, `{{remediation_steps}}`) and test-dispatch modal.\n   - **Email History & Backoff Queue**: Exponential retry tracking (`5m` $\\rightarrow$ `15m` $\\rightarrow$ `1h` $\\rightarrow$ `3h` $\\rightarrow$ `12h`) with manual retry capability.\n   - **Recipient Management**: Distribution lists with email regex validation and subscription filters.\n\n7. **SOC Operations, Auditability & Health Telemetry**\n   - **Searchable Audit Trail**: Categorized audit logs (PIPELINE, SECURITY, FEED, WATCHLIST, AUTH, EMAIL) with CSV/JSON export.\n   - **Health Probes**: Dedicated `/live`, `/health`, and `/ready` status telemetry, Gunicorn multi-worker topology, NTP time drift monitoring, and security headers breakdown (CSP, X-Frame-Options DENY, HSTS, CSRF token validation, 30-min session timeout)."
