  planner_response {
    response: "### VulnStream \342\200\224 Autonomous Product Vulnerability Tracking & Notification System\n\nThe application has been completely redesigned with a **NextUI/HeroUI-inspired professional aesthetic**, all SLA constructs have been removed, and the platform has been tailored for **unattended product vulnerability tracking with zero human intervention**.\n\n---\n\n### Key Updates & Architectural Refinements\n\n1. **NextUI Design Language & Subtle Palette**\n   - **Neutral Zinc Palette**: Replaced flashy, saturated neon colors with a refined enterprise theme (`#09090b` background, `#18181b` card surfaces, subtle `#27272a` borders, and crisp `#f4f4f5` typography).\n   - **NextUI Component Aesthetics**: Refined `rounded-2xl` cards with subtle borders, smooth pill chips for statuses (`AUTO_DISPATCHED`, `CISA KEV`, `CVSS`), minimalist monospaced CVE identifiers, and responsive tab switchers.\n   - **Restrained Visual Density**: Removed flashing alarm banners and pulsating countdowns in favor of clean, quiet status indicators.\n\n2. **Complete Removal of SLA Engine**\n   - **Removed All SLA Tracking**: Purged SLA deadlines, breach timers, SLA tier countdowns, promotion clock resets, and breach warning banners from all views.\n   - **Purged SLA Directives from Advisories & Templates**: Removed `{{sla_hours}}`, `{{sla_deadline}}`, and `{{sla_warning}}` from email templates, bulletins, and PDF export modules.\n   - **Settings Cleanup**: Removed SLA tier duration settings, keeping configuration focused on ingestion windows and autonomous scheduler intervals.\n\n3. **Autonomous Product Tracking & Zero-Human Notification**\n   - **Monitored Product Correlation**: Uses strict **NIST IR 7695 CPE 2.3** component matching with fallback heuristic to monitor products, applications, and operating systems.\n   - **Zero-Touch Automated Dispatch**: Ingested vulnerabilities from NVD, OpenCVE, CISA KEV, GHSA, and EPSS are automatically matched against monitored inventory, generating and dispatching advisories and email notifications immediately without human approval or manual gating.\n   - **Autonomous Pipeline Phases**:\n     1. Feed Ingestion & SSRF Pre-flight Validation (16+ vendor feeds)\n     2. Deduplication & Timeline Scope Filtering ($O(1)$ canonical lookup)\n     3. Multi-Source Auto-Enrichment (CVSS v3.1, EPSS probability, CISA KEV tags)\n     4. Product Watch-List CPE 2.3 Matching\n     5. Instant Automated Notification Dispatch (Mailgun TLS 1.3 / SMTP)\n   - **Notification Ledger & Resend Capability**: Tracks all automatic transmissions in the delivery log and sent registry, with manual resend and exponential backoff retry support (`5m` $\\rightarrow$ `15m` $\\rightarrow$ `1h` $\\rightarrow$ `3h` $\\rightarrow$ `12h`)."
    thinking: "**Verifying Project Requirements**\n\nOkay, both the `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` tasks are complete, with no reported errors, which is great news. I\'m now double-checking everything to ensure that the user\'s initial request is fully addressed. Specifically, I\'ve confirmed the \"React + NextUI UI\" requirement by adopting the NextUI/HeroUI design language, utilizing the neutral zinc-950/zinc-900 palettes.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### VulnStream \342\200\224 Autonomous Product Vulnerability Tracking & Notification System\n\nThe application has been completely redesigned with a **NextUI/HeroUI-inspired professional aesthetic**, all SLA constructs have been removed, and the platform has been tailored for **unattended product vulnerability tracking with zero human intervention**.\n\n---\n\n### Key Updates & Architectural Refinements\n\n1. **NextUI Design Language & Subtle Palette**\n   - **Neutral Zinc Palette**: Replaced flashy, saturated neon colors with a refined enterprise theme (`#09090b` background, `#18181b` card surfaces, subtle `#27272a` borders, and crisp `#f4f4f5` typography).\n   - **NextUI Component Aesthetics**: Refined `rounded-2xl` cards with subtle borders, smooth pill chips for statuses (`AUTO_DISPATCHED`, `CISA KEV`, `CVSS`), minimalist monospaced CVE identifiers, and responsive tab switchers.\n   - **Restrained Visual Density**: Removed flashing alarm banners and pulsating countdowns in favor of clean, quiet status indicators.\n\n2. **Complete Removal of SLA Engine**\n   - **Removed All SLA Tracking**: Purged SLA deadlines, breach timers, SLA tier countdowns, promotion clock resets, and breach warning banners from all views.\n   - **Purged SLA Directives from Advisories & Templates**: Removed `{{sla_hours}}`, `{{sla_deadline}}`, and `{{sla_warning}}` from email templates, bulletins, and PDF export modules.\n   - **Settings Cleanup**: Removed SLA tier duration settings, keeping configuration focused on ingestion windows and autonomous scheduler intervals.\n\n3. **Autonomous Product Tracking & Zero-Human Notification**\n   - **Monitored Product Correlation**: Uses strict **NIST IR 7695 CPE 2.3** component matching with fallback heuristic to monitor products, applications, and operating systems.\n   - **Zero-Touch Automated Dispatch**: Ingested vulnerabilities from NVD, OpenCVE, CISA KEV, GHSA, and EPSS are automatically matched against monitored inventory, generating and dispatching advisories and email notifications immediately without human approval or manual gating.\n   - **Autonomous Pipeline Phases**:\n     1. Feed Ingestion & SSRF Pre-flight Validation (16+ vendor feeds)\n     2. Deduplication & Timeline Scope Filtering ($O(1)$ canonical lookup)\n     3. Multi-Source Auto-Enrichment (CVSS v3.1, EPSS probability, CISA KEV tags)\n     4. Product Watch-List CPE 2.3 Matching\n     5. Instant Automated Notification Dispatch (Mailgun TLS 1.3 / SMTP)\n   - **Notification Ledger & Resend Capability**: Tracks all automatic transmissions in the delivery log and sent registry, with manual resend and exponential backoff retry support (`5m` $\\rightarrow$ `15m` $\\rightarrow$ `1h` $\\rightarrow$ `3h` $\\rightarrow$ `12h`)."
