  planner_response {
    response: "Here are the most valuable enterprise improvements for **VulnStream**, focused on unattended product vulnerability tracking, zero-human-intervention notification, and the NextUI clean design system:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Multi-Channel Autonomous Webhook Routing (Slack, Teams, PagerDuty, Jira)\n* **Current state**: Notifications are dispatched exclusively via email (Mailgun/SMTP).\n* **Improvement**: Add an **Autonomous Notification Routing Matrix**:\n  - **Inbound Webhook Destinations**: Route alerts directly to team channels (e.g., Slack `#sec-netops`, MS Teams, or Discord).\n  - **Automated Incident Creation**: Trigger PagerDuty incidents or generate Jira / ServiceNow tickets automatically when an active CISA KEV exploit is detected, with zero human ticketing needed.\n  - **Per-Product Routing Rules**: Map products to specific team webhooks (e.g., FortiOS $\\rightarrow$ NetOps webhook; Windows Server $\\rightarrow$ Identity Ops webhook).\n\n---\n\n### 2. CPE Version Range & SemVer Comparison (Eliminating False Positives)\n* **Current state**: Matching uses CPE 2.3 component tokens with wildcard `*` matching.\n* **Improvement**: Implement **NVD version range parsing** (`versionStartIncluding`, `versionEndExcluding`):\n  - Automatically evaluate if the deployed product version (e.g., `11.0.4-h1`) is strictly within the vulnerable range ($< 11.0.4$).\n  - Auto-filter already-patched versions before dispatching notifications so inboxes never receive non-impacted alerts.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Patch Tuesday Digest Batching & Rate Limiting\n* **Current state**: Each correlated vulnerability can generate its own notification.\n* **Improvement**: **Intelligent Run Aggregation**:\n  - When vendors release 30+ CVEs simultaneously (e.g., Microsoft Patch Tuesday or Red Hat batch updates), automatically coalesce all matching vulnerabilities into a **Single Consolidated Product Advisory Digest** per asset instead of 30 individual emails.\n  - Prevents mailbox flooding and SMTP provider rate-limiting.\n\n---\n\n### 4. CycloneDX & SPDX Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) Ingestion\n* **Current state**: Products are registered manually or via custom bulk JSON.\n* **Improvement**: Add native **SBOM JSON import**:\n  - Paste or upload standard `cyclonedx.json` or `spdx.json` files generated by CI/CD pipelines (Docker, Syft, Trivy).\n  - Automatically extract all packages, operating systems, and CPEs directly into the monitored product watch-list.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Automated Noise Reduction & Environmental Suppression Rules\n* **Current state**: All matching CVEs generate alerts.\n* **Improvement**: Configurable unattended suppression filters:\n  - **Attack Vector Suppression**: Automatically mute vulnerabilities requiring physical access (`AV:P`) or local adjacent access (`AV:A`) if the asset is classified as `CLOUD_INFRA`.\n  - **EPSS Confidence Gate**: Option to only auto-dispatch for vulnerabilities with EPSS probability $> 10\\%$ unless CVSS is Critical.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Interactive Notification Dry-Run / Test Inspector\n* **Current state**: Notifications dispatch during pipeline execution.\n* **Improvement**: A **\"Test Ingestion Simulator\"** tab:\n  - Paste any sample CVE ID or raw JSON advisory to preview which monitored products match, which webhooks would fire, and examine the exact rendered payload before the live scheduler processes it.\n\n---\n\n### Which of these would you like to implement first?\n1. **Multi-Channel Webhooks (Slack / Teams / PagerDuty / Webhook URL dispatch)**\n2. **CPE Version Range Matching (SemVer comparison for zero false-positives)**\n3. **Consolidated Digest Batching (prevents email flooding during multi-CVE releases)**\n4. **SBOM Upload (CycloneDX / SPDX JSON import into product inventory)**\n5. **Noise Reduction & Attack Vector Suppression Rules**"
    thinking: "**Identifying Improvements**\n\nI\'m focusing on the current application state to suggest improvements. I\'m prioritizing realistic, high-value, enterprise-grade changes, starting with product vulnerabilities. My goal is to identify specific areas for enhancements.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Enhancement Ideas**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on high-impact improvements, especially regarding autonomous dispatch and notification routing. My latest focus involves creating a flexible Autonomous Webhook & Notification Routing Matrix. This will let us auto-dispatch alerts to multiple channels based on product-specific rules and vulnerability characteristics. I\'m also delving into CPE 2.3 wildcard and semantic version range matching for improved accuracy.\n\n\n**Refining Matching & Filtering**\n\nI\'m expanding the alert filtering capabilities. I\'m incorporating precise version range evaluation alongside CPE 2.3 matching to eliminate false positives on patched versions. Also, I\'m working on autonomous rules to suppress non-actionable alerts based on attack vector or EPSS scores, aiming to maintain clean notification inboxes and prevent alert fatigue. Lastly, I\'m building a Dry-Run Ingestion Tester to simulate CVEs and security bulletins, for distribution channel and message preview. I\'m also planning notification throttling.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Here are the most valuable enterprise improvements for **VulnStream**, focused on unattended product vulnerability tracking, zero-human-intervention notification, and the NextUI clean design system:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Multi-Channel Autonomous Webhook Routing (Slack, Teams, PagerDuty, Jira)\n* **Current state**: Notifications are dispatched exclusively via email (Mailgun/SMTP).\n* **Improvement**: Add an **Autonomous Notification Routing Matrix**:\n  - **Inbound Webhook Destinations**: Route alerts directly to team channels (e.g., Slack `#sec-netops`, MS Teams, or Discord).\n  - **Automated Incident Creation**: Trigger PagerDuty incidents or generate Jira / ServiceNow tickets automatically when an active CISA KEV exploit is detected, with zero human ticketing needed.\n  - **Per-Product Routing Rules**: Map products to specific team webhooks (e.g., FortiOS $\\rightarrow$ NetOps webhook; Windows Server $\\rightarrow$ Identity Ops webhook).\n\n---\n\n### 2. CPE Version Range & SemVer Comparison (Eliminating False Positives)\n* **Current state**: Matching uses CPE 2.3 component tokens with wildcard `*` matching.\n* **Improvement**: Implement **NVD version range parsing** (`versionStartIncluding`, `versionEndExcluding`):\n  - Automatically evaluate if the deployed product version (e.g., `11.0.4-h1`) is strictly within the vulnerable range ($< 11.0.4$).\n  - Auto-filter already-patched versions before dispatching notifications so inboxes never receive non-impacted alerts.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Patch Tuesday Digest Batching & Rate Limiting\n* **Current state**: Each correlated vulnerability can generate its own notification.\n* **Improvement**: **Intelligent Run Aggregation**:\n  - When vendors release 30+ CVEs simultaneously (e.g., Microsoft Patch Tuesday or Red Hat batch updates), automatically coalesce all matching vulnerabilities into a **Single Consolidated Product Advisory Digest** per asset instead of 30 individual emails.\n  - Prevents mailbox flooding and SMTP provider rate-limiting.\n\n---\n\n### 4. CycloneDX & SPDX Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) Ingestion\n* **Current state**: Products are registered manually or via custom bulk JSON.\n* **Improvement**: Add native **SBOM JSON import**:\n  - Paste or upload standard `cyclonedx.json` or `spdx.json` files generated by CI/CD pipelines (Docker, Syft, Trivy).\n  - Automatically extract all packages, operating systems, and CPEs directly into the monitored product watch-list.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Automated Noise Reduction & Environmental Suppression Rules\n* **Current state**: All matching CVEs generate alerts.\n* **Improvement**: Configurable unattended suppression filters:\n  - **Attack Vector Suppression**: Automatically mute vulnerabilities requiring physical access (`AV:P`) or local adjacent access (`AV:A`) if the asset is classified as `CLOUD_INFRA`.\n  - **EPSS Confidence Gate**: Option to only auto-dispatch for vulnerabilities with EPSS probability $> 10\\%$ unless CVSS is Critical.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Interactive Notification Dry-Run / Test Inspector\n* **Current state**: Notifications dispatch during pipeline execution.\n* **Improvement**: A **\"Test Ingestion Simulator\"** tab:\n  - Paste any sample CVE ID or raw JSON advisory to preview which monitored products match, which webhooks would fire, and examine the exact rendered payload before the live scheduler processes it.\n\n---\n\n### Which of these would you like to implement first?\n1. **Multi-Channel Webhooks (Slack / Teams / PagerDuty / Webhook URL dispatch)**\n2. **CPE Version Range Matching (SemVer comparison for zero false-positives)**\n3. **Consolidated Digest Batching (prevents email flooding during multi-CVE releases)**\n4. **SBOM Upload (CycloneDX / SPDX JSON import into product inventory)**\n5. **Noise Reduction & Attack Vector Suppression Rules**"
