  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "{\"step_index\":1,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:42:29Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nbuild a modern application, enterprise grade Multi-source feed ingestion \342\200\224 normalizes and deduplicates CVEs from NVD, OpenCVE, CISA KEV, GHSA, OSV, VulCheck, and EPSS enrichment data into a unified record format.\\n\\nConfigurable threat feed management \342\200\224 admins can add/edit/delete custom RSS/Atom, STIX 2.x, TAXII 2.1, GitHub Advisory, and JSON Search API feed sources with per-feed auth (API key, bearer, basic) and rate limiting. Includes 16 pre-seeded vendor feeds (Microsoft, Fortinet, Cisco\\n<truncated 4577 bytes>\\nps \342\200\224 custom-format PostgreSQL dumps with selective restore support\\nEmail \342\200\224 Mailgun delivery disabled by default; graceful degradation when disabled\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-19T23:42:29-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-4bmuxvetm2tba5elubuyrh-950371923494.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-4bmuxvetm2tba5elubuyrh-950371923494.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: alamgir9@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":2,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:42:29Z\",\"input_tokens\":21135,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1511,\"thinking\":\"**Assessing Core Capabilities**\\n\\nI\'m considering the comprehensive Vulnerability Intelligence platform, encompassing ingestion, matching, classification, and remediation. I\'m focusing on its enterprise-grade nature and how it aligns with critical standards and tracking capabilities. The platform includes a Security Operations component as well. I am now beginning an assessment of core skills.\\n\\n\\n**Inspecting Required Features**\\n\\nI\'m now prioritizing the concrete features to implement. The specification focus\\n<truncated 2152 bytes>\\n I\'m focusing on the threat feed management capabilities, including connectivity testing, health stats, and comprehensive source integration and customization. I\'m also addressing recipient management with email validation and subscription tiers, and designing an editable advisory template with live preview and test capabilities. I\'m also now focusing on system settings, operational logs, and system health status. Finally, I am implementing user profile and security features, including password policies.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/metadata.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading metadata.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read metadata\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":4,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:42:45Z\",\"input_tokens\":3880,\"cache_read_tokens\":19594,\"output_tokens\":144,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/package.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading package.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read package.json\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":6,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:42:50Z\",\"input_tokens\":2946,\"cache_read_tokens\":21360,\"output_tokens\":513,\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Dev Server Configuration**\\n\\nI\'m verifying the dev server runs with `vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0`. I\'m checking Vite\'s ability to run as a React SPA with a client-side mock/engine, and also exploring clean execution within the React application, which allows for robust state management, mock storage, realistic live pipeline execution, and CPE matching.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update metadata.json with app title and description\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"6\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Set name and description for the Vulnerability Intelligence & Ingestion Platform\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"VulnStream Enterprise \342\200\224 Vulnerability Intelligence & Pipeline\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Multi-source CVE threat feed ingestion, CPE-first watch-list matching, priority SLA classification, remediation generation, and advisory orchestratio\\n<truncated 117 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"requestFramePermissions\\\\\\\": [],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"majorCapabilities\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\\\\\\\"]\\\\n}\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/metadata.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating metadata.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update app metadata\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":8,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:42:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":2924,\"cache_read_tokens\":22275,\"output_tokens\":538,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update index.html with app title, description, and JetBrains Mono / Inter font links\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"16\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Set app title and meta tags\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"    <title>VulnStream Enterprise \342\200\224 Threat Feed Ingestion & Vulnerability Intelligence</title>\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"Multi-source CVE threat feed ingestion, CPE-first watch-list matching, priority SLA classification, remediation gener\\n<truncated 832 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"5\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta property=\\\\\\\"og:title\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"My Google AI Studio App\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta property=\\\\\\\"og:description\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"\\n<truncated 183 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/index.html\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating index.html metadata\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update HTML head and title\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":10,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:43:01Z\",\"input_tokens\":3274,\"cache_read_tokens\":23075,\"output_tokens\":4599,\"thinking\":\"**Examining Styling Choices**\\n\\nI\'m currently reviewing `src/index.css`. The presence of `@import \\\"tailwindcss\\\";` suggests a strong styling foundation. Now, I\'m focusing on enhancements for a polished cybersecurity console. My priorities are to optimize typography, fine-tune font families, implement dark background styling, and customize scrollbars. The goal is a top-tier, crisp aesthetic.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Data Structures**\\n\\nI\'ve moved on to defining the core data structures needed for the console, starting with\\n<truncated 5577 bytes>\\nrecipient lists, assigning roles and tiers, and tracking delivery success. I\'m also planning the advisory template, a live visual editor with variable tokens and preview capabilities for desktop and mobile clients. I\'m integrating email delivery logs with retry queues and bounce status visualization. I am also working on operational logs for auditing and system health checks, including SSRF protection and CSRF token monitoring. Furthermore, I\'m working on configurable scope hours and scheduler intervals.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Configure styling with Tailwind font families and custom dark theme scrollbars\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"2\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add base styling and font classes\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"@import \\\\\\\"tailwindcss\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n@layer base {\\\\n  body {\\\\n    font-family: \'Plus Jakarta Sans\', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \\\\\\\"Segoe UI\\\\\\\", Roboto, sans-serif;\\\\n    background-color: #0b0f17;\\\\n    color: #e2e8f0;\\\\n    overflow-x: hidden;\\\\n  }\\\\n\\\\n  code, p\\n<truncated 358 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"@import \\\\\\\"tailwindcss\\\\\\\";\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Configure base styles and dark theme scrollbars\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":12,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:43:35Z\",\"input_tokens\":5376,\"cache_read_tokens\":27485,\"output_tokens\":2994,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Application Architecture**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on systematically building the application\'s architecture. The initial step involves defining all domain types in `src/types/index.ts`. This covers everything from CPE 2.3 and CISA KEV to EPSS, SLA tiers, feed types, deduplication, pipelines, findings, advisories, email logs, health checks, and security headers.\\n\\n\\n**Building Core Components**\\n\\nI\'ve been concentrating on essential utilities. Specifically, I\'ve created the CPE 2.3 parser and matcher (`sr\\n<truncated 703 bytes>\\nhich will now also feature instant PDF export.\\n\\n\\n**Constructing Feature Views**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on building the application\'s feature-specific views. I\'m implementing a JSON download for pipeline reports. Also, I\'m working on views for alerted CVE history, threat feeds with custom feed creators, recipients management with email validation, an advisory template editor, email history with retry mechanisms, operational logs, system health checks, and a settings view for scope hours and SLA configurations.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"export type Severity = \'CRITICAL\' | \'HIGH\' | \'MEDIUM\' | \'LOW\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type ExposureLevel = \\\\n  | \'INTERNET_FACING\' \\\\n  | \'INTERNAL_CRITICAL\' \\\\n  | \'DMZ\' \\\\n  | \'WORKSTATION\' \\\\n  | \'CLOUD_INFRA\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type PriorityTier = \\\\n  | \'P0_CISA_KEV\' \\\\n  | \'P\\n<truncated 5993 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create core domain TypeScript interfaces and types\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types/index.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating types file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create types file\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":14,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:43:54Z\",\"input_tokens\":3332,\"cache_read_tokens\":33012,\"output_tokens\":2079,\"thinking\":\"**Defining CPE Matcher Utility**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on the CPE Matcher utility\'s implementation. The specifications demand a strict CPE 2.3 matching approach, prioritizing watch-list entries. It will need to support fallback to vendor/product matching when the CPE match fails. Multi-CPE entries per watch-list item are also required.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * CPE 2.3 Strict Component Matcher & Vendor/Product Fallback\\\\n * Spec: NIST Interagency Report 7695 (Common Platform Enumeration: Naming Specification Version 2.3)\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nexport interface ParsedCPE {\\\\n  prefix: string; // cpe:2.3\\\\n  part: string;  \\n<truncated 5361 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement CPE 2.3 strict component matcher, fallback heuristic, and auto-resolver\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/utils/cpeMatcher.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating cpeMatcher.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create CPE matcher utility\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":16,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:44:09Z\",\"input_tokens\":2351,\"cache_read_tokens\":36261,\"output_tokens\":961,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Deduplication System**\\n\\nI\'m now building `src/utils/deduplicator.ts`. Key features include canonical CVE ID normalization for validation and uppercase format, along with time-based scope filtering using `scope_hours`. I will also be implementing O(1) deduplication to ensure efficient processing.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * CVE ID Normalization and Deduplication Engine\\\\n * Enforces canonical CVE-YYYY-NNNN+ format and O(1) tracking.\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nconst CVE_REGEX = /^CVE-\\\\\\\\d{4}-\\\\\\\\d{4,}$/i;\\\\n\\\\n/**\\\\n * Normalizes any CVE string into canonical uppercase, trimmed format.\\\\n * Ret\\n<truncated 2454 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement canonical CVE normalizer and in-run O(1) deduplicator with timeline scope filtering\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/utils/deduplicator.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating deduplicator.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create deduplicator utility\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":18,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:44:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":3343,\"cache_read_tokens\":36412,\"output_tokens\":18718,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Seed Data Requirements**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on the initial data requirements, specifically the seed data for the application. My current thought is to define the necessary structure for 16 pre-seeded vendor feeds. I\'m starting to list the feeds, with Microsoft, Fortinet, Cisco, and VMware/Broadcom as the initial candidates. I\'ll need to figure out data formats and structures soon.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding Data Sources**\\n\\nI\'ve expanded the seed data sources. I\'m now exploring security advisory feeds. I\'m inco\\n<truncated 348 bytes>\\nrtiOS SSL-VPN, Palo Alto Networks PAN-OS GlobalProtect, and Cisco IOS XE/ASA.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Vulnerability Data**\\n\\nI\'m now diving deeper into vulnerability data. I\'m focusing on incorporating Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVEs). I\'ve decided to prioritize a normalized CVE corpus, including CISA KEV entries with a 6-hour SLA. I am specifically considering vulnerabilities in PAN-OS, FortiOS, Windows, OpenSSH, Cisco ASA, VMware ESXi, PHP, and TeamCity. I\'m assessing the CVE data points for each entry.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import {\\\\n  ThreatFeed,\\\\n  WatchListItem,\\\\n  NormalizedCVE,\\\\n  Finding,\\\\n  Advisory,\\\\n  AlertedCVE,\\\\n  EmailRecipient,\\\\n  EmailDeliveryLog,\\\\n  AuditLog,\\\\n  AppSettings,\\\\n} from \'../types\';\\\\n\\\\nexport const INITIAL_FEEDS: ThreatFeed[] = [\\\\n  {\\\\n    id: \'fee\\n<truncated 47768 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create pre-seeded feeds, watch list, authentic CVE intelligence dataset, findings, and advisories\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/data/seedData.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating seedData.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create seed data for vulnerability engine\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":20,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:46:12Z\",\"input_tokens\":19773,\"cache_read_tokens\":39139,\"output_tokens\":5579,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Ingestion Pipeline**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on building the Pipeline Engine in `src/engine/pipelineEngine.ts`. The initial specification involves multi-source feed ingestion. I am normalizing and deduplicating CVEs from various sources: NVD, OpenCVE, CISA KEV, GHSA, OSV, VulCheck, and EPSS enrichment data into unified records.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Threat Feed Handling**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into threat feed management. This includes implementing rate limiting, various authentication methods, and latency tracking. SSRF protection is a priority, rejecting private IPs, loopback, link-local, and credential exposures. I\'m building this using a watch-list matching system that prioritizes CPE 2.3 components, with fallback to vendor/product matching. I\'m also implementing multi-CPE entries.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import {\\\\n  ThreatFeed,\\\\n  WatchListItem,\\\\n  NormalizedCVE,\\\\n  Finding,\\\\n  Advisory,\\\\n  AlertedCVE,\\\\n  PipelineExecution,\\\\n  PipelinePhase,\\\\n  AppSettings,\\\\n  PriorityTier,\\\\n  EmailDeliveryLog,\\\\n  AuditLog,\\\\n} from \'../types\';\\\\nimport { normalizeCveId, is\\n<truncated 16918 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement pipeline runner engine with feed ingestion, SSRF validation, enrichment, CPE matching, priority classification, and advisory dispatch\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/engine/pipelineEngine.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating pipelineEngine.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create pipeline engine\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":22,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:46:50Z\",\"input_tokens\":5974,\"cache_read_tokens\":58808,\"output_tokens\":7453,\"thinking\":\"**Building Context Structure**\\n\\nI\'m currently structuring the React Context and state management in `src/context/AppContext.tsx`. My focus is on defining the necessary features. Right now, I\'m setting up state for the feeds. I\'ll need a list to store them (pre-seeded and custom), functions to add new feeds, edit existing ones, and delete feeds.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding Feature Details**\\n\\nNow I\'m diving deeper into the specifics. I\'m focusing on adding the ability to toggle enable/disable, test connectivity (including pings, latency updates, and an SSRF check). I\'m also planning the watch list state, considering items, adding assets with CPE validation, and bulk JSON import. I have begun to plan state around findings and threat data, including live SLA calculations, and I\'ve started thinking about advisory exports and CVE re-alerting.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { createContext, useContext, useState, useEffect, useMemo, useCallback } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  ThreatFeed,\\\\n  WatchListItem,\\\\n  NormalizedCVE,\\\\n  Finding,\\\\n  Advisory,\\\\n  AlertedCVE,\\\\n  EmailRecipient,\\\\n  EmailDeliveryLog,\\\\n  AuditLog,\\\\\\n<truncated 24380 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create complete AppContext for reactive state management, pipeline triggers, SLA tickers, and SOC operations\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/context/AppContext.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating AppContext.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create app context\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":24,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:47:36Z\",\"input_tokens\":7916,\"cache_read_tokens\":64616,\"output_tokens\":5959,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing UI Elements**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on building the UI components, specifically the views outlined in the user prompt. I\'m starting with the top header and navigation bar. It\'ll feature the \\\"VulnStream Enterprise\\\" branding and a high-density cyber emblem. I\'m also planning to implement a real-time SLA breach ticker banner.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Status Indicators**\\n\\nI\'ve been working on the status indicators for the UI. I\'ve defined indicators for pipeline status, NTP sync, CSRF token, session timeou\\n<truncated 3710 bytes>\\nity.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Operational Logs**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on the OperationalLogsView. I\'m building a comprehensive, searchable audit trail with filters for Category and Level, and export options as CSV/JSON. I\'m moving on to the SystemHealthView, checking for process and dependency health. I\'m also ensuring readiness with a multi-worker-safe status check, and considering SSRF protection and security header audits. Finally, I\'m working on the SettingsView to allow scope hour customization, using a slider.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  ShieldAlert,\\\\n  Radio,\\\\n  Clock,\\\\n  Play,\\\\n  RotateCw,\\\\n  Server,\\\\n  KeyRound,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  AlertTriangle,\\\\n  Flame,\\\\n  Activity,\\\\n  Layers,\\\\n  C\\n<truncated 13074 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement TopHeader with SLA urgency alerts, pipeline triggers, scope selector, session countdown, and SOC sub-nav tabs\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/TopHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating TopHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create top navigation header\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":26,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:48:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":6414,\"cache_read_tokens\":73197,\"output_tokens\":5931,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing DashboardView.tsx**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on building `DashboardView.tsx` based on the provided specifications. I\'m starting with the vulnerability statistics components, aiming to incorporate Total Assets Monitored, Open Findings, CISA KEV In Wild data, and SLA Status. I also plan to include a section displaying the status of Feeds Online, keeping in mind the need for clear and concise visual representation.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  ShieldAlert,\\\\n  Flame,\\\\n  AlertOctagon,\\\\n  Clock,\\\\n  Radio,\\\\n  FileText,\\\\n  Server,\\\\n  ArrowUpRight,\\\\n  TrendingUp,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  Exter\\n<truncated 20266 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement DashboardView with KPI stats, SLA countdown urgency matrix, asset exposure radar, and ingestion flow summary\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/DashboardView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating DashboardView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create dashboard view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":28,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:48:52Z\",\"input_tokens\":6366,\"cache_read_tokens\":79380,\"output_tokens\":7469,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Watch List Functionality**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the implementation of `WatchListView.tsx`. I\'m starting by reviewing the requirements related to the watch list\'s matching functionality. This includes strict CPE 2.3 component matching, with vendor/product fallback, and the ability to handle multiple CPE entries per watch list item, resolving them automatically using the NVD.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport { WatchListItem, ExposureLevel } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport { generateCPE23, parseCPE23 } from \'../utils/cpeMatcher\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Server,\\\\n  Plus,\\\\n  Upload,\\\\\\n<truncated 27341 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement WatchListView with strict CPE 2.3 inventory, generator, editor, and bulk JSON import (max 1000 items)\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WatchListView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating WatchListView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create watch list view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":30,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:49:36Z\",\"input_tokens\":7956,\"cache_read_tokens\":85453,\"output_tokens\":8005,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing FindingsView**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into building `FindingsView.tsx`. The core functionality will focus on triage, filtering, and prioritizing vulnerabilities, incorporating a remediation workflow. I\'m also ensuring the inclusion of priority classification, specifically incorporating CISA KEV data, which will take 6 hours to incorporate.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Remediation Workflow**\\n\\nI\'ve just added detailed remediation instructions. These include vendor patch URLs, immediate actions, workarounds, rollback plans, and step-by-step instructions. Also, I\'m integrating SLA tracking for each finding\'s SLA deadlines (CISA KEV: 6h, Critical: 24h, High: 72h, Medium: 168h), breach detection, and clock-reset on tier promotions. I\'m also planning the status transitions.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport { Finding, PriorityTier, FindingStatus, ExposureLevel } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  ShieldAlert,\\\\n  Flame,\\\\n  AlertTriangle,\\\\n  Clock,\\\\n  CheckC\\n<truncated 29789 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement FindingsView with priority SLA classification, live countdowns, triage status workflow, and comprehensive remediation playbook drawer\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/FindingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating FindingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create findings view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":32,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:50:21Z\",\"input_tokens\":8499,\"cache_read_tokens\":93204,\"output_tokens\":3265,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Threat Data View**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into building `ThreatDataView.tsx`. The goal is to inspect normalized threat intelligence and enrich the NVD batch data by filling missing CVSS scores. This view should offer a clear and concise look at the cached threat feed.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport { NormalizedCVE } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Database,\\\\n  Search,\\\\n  Filter,\\\\n  Flame,\\\\n  ExternalLink,\\\\n  Code,\\\\n  FileJson,\\\\n  Layers,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\\\n<truncated 10746 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement ThreatDataView to inspect normalized threat intelligence cache with NVD CVSS, EPSS percentiles, CISA KEV tags, and raw JSON modal\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ThreatDataView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating ThreatDataView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create threat data view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":34,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:50:40Z\",\"input_tokens\":3541,\"cache_read_tokens\":101602,\"output_tokens\":4352,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing AdvisoriesView**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m diving into building `AdvisoriesView.tsx`. The core functionality will involve displaying a list of generated advisories, complete with their delivery status, the CVEs they affect, and a PDF export option. I need to consider using WeasyPrint or ReportLab as a fallback for PDF generation. The display will include information like `ADV-202`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport { Advisory } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  FileText,\\\\n  Download,\\\\n  Printer,\\\\n  Copy,\\\\n  Check,\\\\n  ExternalLink,\\\\n  ShieldAlert,\\\\n  Clock,\\\\n  Send,\\\\n  X,\\\\n \\n<truncated 14819 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement AdvisoriesView with security bulletin cards, PDF export generation, JSON download, and Markdown copy\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/AdvisoriesView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating AdvisoriesView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create advisories view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":36,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:51:05Z\",\"input_tokens\":4672,\"cache_read_tokens\":105026,\"output_tokens\":3498,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing The UI**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into building `PipelineExecutionsView.tsx`. The goal is a live execution flow, showing phase progress: fetch, enrich, classify, persist, and deliver. I\'m also including a feature for downloading pipeline output reports as JSON.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Play,\\\\n  RotateCw,\\\\n  Clock,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  AlertTriangle,\\\\n  Download,\\\\n  Terminal,\\\\n  Activity,\\\\n  Layers,\\\\n  FileJson,\\\\n  Zap,\\\\n} from \'lucide-r\\n<truncated 11856 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement PipelineExecutionsView showing phase progress, ingestion counters, duration telemetry, and raw JSON export\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/PipelineExecutionsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating PipelineExecutionsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create pipeline executions view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":38,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:51:26Z\",\"input_tokens\":3778,\"cache_read_tokens\":109595,\"output_tokens\":2586,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing AlertedCVEsView**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into building `AlertedCVEsView.tsx`. The core functionality focuses on tracking and managing CVEs that have already been sent to recipients, including re-alerting options post-remediation. My current focus is on implementing deduplication using canonical CVE ID normalization, ensuring an O(1) lookup against the previously alerted list.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport { AlertedCVE } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Bell,\\\\n  RotateCcw,\\\\n  Search,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  Clock,\\\\n  ShieldCheck,\\\\n  Mail,\\\\n  AlertTriangle,\\\\n  X,\\\\n} fr\\n<truncated 8466 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement AlertedCVEsView with tracking table, suppression registry, and re-alerting modal with SLA clock reset\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/AlertedCVEsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating AlertedCVEsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create alerted CVEs view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":40,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:51:43Z\",\"input_tokens\":2827,\"cache_read_tokens\":113332,\"output_tokens\":5172,\"thinking\":\"**Building ThreatFeedsView**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the implementation of `ThreatFeedsView.tsx`. The goal is a comprehensive threat feed management interface. Currently, I\'m focusing on the specifications, specifically the admin-level control over various feed sources: RSS/Atom, STIX 2.x, TAXII 2.1, GitHub Advisory, and JSON Search APIs. I need to make these sources configurable.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport { ThreatFeed, FeedType, FeedAuthType } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Radio,\\\\n  Plus,\\\\n  Play,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  AlertTriangle,\\\\n  Lock,\\\\n  Trash2,\\\\n  Edit2\\n<truncated 18528 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement ThreatFeedsView with 16 pre-seeded feeds, custom feed management, SSRF checks, and ping connectivity tester\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ThreatFeedsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating ThreatFeedsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create threat feeds view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":42,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:52:15Z\",\"input_tokens\":5514,\"cache_read_tokens\":116024,\"output_tokens\":3307,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing New Views**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on building the remaining views. I\'m currently prioritizing `RecipientsView.tsx`, which handles security distributions, roles, and validation. After that, I\'ll tackle `AdvisoryTemplateView.tsx`, with its editable HTML template and live preview. Finally, I\'ll implement the `EmailHistoryView.tsx` for notification delivery.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport { EmailRecipient } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Users,\\\\n  Plus,\\\\n  Trash2,\\\\n  Mail,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  AlertCircle,\\\\n  X,\\\\n  Search,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\'\\n<truncated 11350 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement RecipientsView for managing security distribution list with email validation and subscription tiers\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/RecipientsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating RecipientsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create recipients view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":44,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:52:35Z\",\"input_tokens\":3570,\"cache_read_tokens\":121473,\"output_tokens\":3194,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Advisory Template**\\n\\nI\'m focusing on building the `AdvisoryTemplateView.tsx` component. The core requirement is an editable HTML email template that includes a live preview and the ability to test-send the template to a configured recipient. I\'m noting the necessary variable tags too, like `{{advisory_id}}` and `{{advisory_title}}` for dynamic content.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  FileCode,\\\\n  Send,\\\\n  Eye,\\\\n  RotateCcw,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  AlertCircle,\\\\n  Copy,\\\\n  Check,\\\\n  Code,\\\\n  X,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { INITIAL_AD\\n<truncated 10359 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement AdvisoryTemplateView with code editor, variable tokens, live email client preview iframe, and test send modal\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/AdvisoryTemplateView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating AdvisoryTemplateView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create advisory template view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":46,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:52:56Z\",\"input_tokens\":3452,\"cache_read_tokens\":124986,\"output_tokens\":2336,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Email History**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into building `EmailHistoryView.tsx`. The goal is to display email delivery attempts, along with provider status and retry tracking, as outlined in the specifications. I\'m focusing on the \\\"Autonomous Operation: Retry with backoff \342\200\224 pipeline\\\" aspect to ensure efficient handling of delivery failures.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Mail,\\\\n  RotateCw,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  AlertTriangle,\\\\n  Clock,\\\\n  Search,\\\\n  ExternalLink,\\\\n  ShieldCheck,\\\\n  Send,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\n\\\\nexport c\\n<truncated 7723 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement EmailHistoryView for tracking notification deliveries, exponential backoff retries, and manual retry triggers\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/EmailHistoryView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating EmailHistoryView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create email history view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":48,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:53:12Z\",\"input_tokens\":2558,\"cache_read_tokens\":128402,\"output_tokens\":2717,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Operational Logs**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on constructing `OperationalLogsView.tsx`. The goal is a searchable audit trail encompassing system, pipeline, email, and security events. I\'m structuring the logs by category: PIPELINE, SECURITY, and FEED. I believe this categorization will significantly improve usability.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport { AuditLog } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  FileCode2,\\\\n  Search,\\\\n  Filter,\\\\n  Download,\\\\n  AlertTriangle,\\\\n  Info,\\\\n  ShieldAlert,\\\\n  Flame,\\\\n  CheckCircle2\\n<truncated 9236 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement OperationalLogsView with category/level filters, search, and CSV/JSON export\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/OperationalLogsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating OperationalLogsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create operational logs view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":50,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:53:28Z\",\"input_tokens\":2953,\"cache_read_tokens\":130904,\"output_tokens\":3213,\"thinking\":\"**Defining System Health Checks**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on defining the components needed for `SystemHealthView.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m thinking through the different health check endpoints: `/live`, `/health`, and `/ready`. I\'m breaking down what each endpoint should report on, like process-level health versus dependency health and strict readiness criteria.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Activity,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  AlertTriangle,\\\\n  ShieldCheck,\\\\n  Server,\\\\n  Lock,\\\\n  Database,\\\\n  Cpu,\\\\n  Clock,\\\\n  RotateCw,\\\\n  Terminal,\\\\n} from \'lucid\\n<truncated 9415 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement SystemHealthView displaying /live, /health, /ready status, multi-worker safety, and security header compliance matrix\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/SystemHealthView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating SystemHealthView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create system health view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":52,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:53:48Z\",\"input_tokens\":3467,\"cache_read_tokens\":133792,\"output_tokens\":5113,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing SettingsView**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the construction of `SettingsView.tsx`. The specifications highlight key areas: database configuration, scheduler and NTP tuning, email (specifically Mailgun) setup, and timezone/date formatting. Additionally, I\'m focusing on advisory number prefixes. I\'m also considering the timeline scope filtering, which includes configurable `scope_hours` with a default of 24h, and checks for published/modified criteria.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useApp } from \'../context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Sliders,\\\\n  Clock,\\\\n  Mail,\\\\n  Shield,\\\\n  KeyRound,\\\\n  Database,\\\\n  Check,\\\\n  AlertCircle,\\\\n  RotateCcw,\\\\n  Save,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\n\\\\nexport cons\\n<truncated 18087 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement SettingsView for SLA tuning, scope hours, scheduler/NTP config, Mailgun settings, and operator credentials hardening\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create settings view\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":54,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:54:18Z\",\"input_tokens\":5435,\"cache_read_tokens\":137148,\"output_tokens\":1261,\"thinking\":\"**Integrating the App**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on connecting all the components within `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve outlined the necessary structure: an `AppProvider` wrapper, a `TopHeader` including SLA urgency, session time, pipeline status, and tabs. I\'m moving on to building out the active view switcher, starting with the dashboard.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { AppProvider, useApp } from \'./context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport { TopHeader } from \'./components/TopHeader\';\\\\nimport { DashboardView } from \'./components/DashboardView\';\\\\nimport { WatchListView } from \'./components/WatchLis\\n<truncated 3125 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Connect all views and AppProvider into src/App.tsx with clean layout, SOC banner, and footer\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Wire application layout and views\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":56,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:54:27Z\",\"input_tokens\":3562,\"cache_read_tokens\":140469,\"output_tokens\":47,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet to verify build\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":58,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:54:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":2272,\"cache_read_tokens\":141888,\"output_tokens\":63,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Linting codebase\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Lint applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":60,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:54:35Z\",\"input_tokens\":2419,\"cache_read_tokens\":142012,\"output_tokens\":326,\"thinking\":\"**Inspecting Lucide Icons**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on rectifying a minor TypeScript discrepancy within `src/components/FindingsView.tsx` at line 254. It seems Lucide icons don\'t directly accept the `title` prop. Therefore, my current solution is to either wrap the icon in a span that uses the title attribute, or eliminate it altogether. My goal is to streamline the code by finding the best approach.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Wrap Lucide Flame icon in a span with title attribute\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"258\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Remove title prop from Lucide icon and put on wrapper\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"                              {finding.cve.cisaKev.isKev && (\\\\n                                <span title=\\\\\\\"CISA KEV Catalog\\\\\\\">\\\\n                                  <Flame className=\\\\\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5 text-amber-400 animate-pulse\\\\\\\" />\\\\n                         \\n<truncated 49 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"252\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"                              {finding.cve.cisaKev.isKev && (\\\\n                                <Flame className=\\\\\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5 text-amber-400 animate-pulse\\\\\\\" title=\\\\\\\"CISA KEV Catalog\\\\\\\" />\\\\n                              )}\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/FindingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"TargetLintErrorIds\":\"[\\\"TS2322\\\"]\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Fixing Lucide icon title prop\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Fix Lucide title typing issue\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":62,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:54:40Z\",\"input_tokens\":2871,\"cache_read_tokens\":142359,\"output_tokens\":49,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Re-linting applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Re-lint applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":64,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:54:44Z\",\"input_tokens\":2294,\"cache_read_tokens\":143086,\"output_tokens\":56,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running final compile verification\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Verify final build\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":66,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T06:54:48Z\",\"input_tokens\":2281,\"cache_read_tokens\":143237,\"output_tokens\":1114,\"content\":\"### VulnStream Enterprise \342\200\224 Vulnerability Intelligence & Ingestion Platform\\n\\nA modern, enterprise-grade threat feed ingestion, CPE-first watch-list correlation, and autonomous SLA tracking platform designed for SOC and incident response teams.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Core Architectural Features Built\\n\\n1. **Multi-Source Threat Feed Ingestion & SSRF Protection**\\n   - **Unified Record Normalization**: Merges NVD CVE 2.0, OpenCVE, CISA KEV, GitHub Advisory Database (GHSA), OSV, VulCheck, and FIRST.org EPSS enrichment into \\n<truncated 3041 bytes>\\nstribution lists with email regex validation and subscription filters.\\n\\n7. **SOC Operations, Auditability & Health Telemetry**\\n   - **Searchable Audit Trail**: Categorized audit logs (PIPELINE, SECURITY, FEED, WATCHLIST, AUTH, EMAIL) with CSV/JSON export.\\n   - **Health Probes**: Dedicated `/live`, `/health`, and `/ready` status telemetry, Gunicorn multi-worker topology, NTP time drift monitoring, and security headers breakdown (CSP, X-Frame-Options DENY, HSTS, CSRF token validation, 30-min session timeout).\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":67,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:00:51Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nReact + NextUI UI, remove SLA. this application is used for tracking products vulnerbilities and sending notification with no human intervention. UI should be professional not wih flashy colors.\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T00:00:51-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-4bmuxvetm2tba5elubuyrh-950371923494.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-4bmuxvetm2tba5elubuyrh-950371923494.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: alamgir9@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":68,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:00:51Z\",\"input_tokens\":146851,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":4051,\"thinking\":\"**Prioritizing UI Simplicity**\\n\\nI\'m focusing on the technical stack for a vulnerabilities tracking and notification application. React with NextUI seems like a solid, efficient choice for the front end, particularly given the need for a professional look and feel. The Service Level Agreement (SLA) component is out. My priority is a clean, automated UI without distracting aesthetics.\\n\\n\\n**Refining UI Aesthetics**\\n\\nI\'m now diving deeper into the UI aesthetics, specifically focusing on achieving a clean, profes\\n<truncated 2782 bytes>\\nions. Also, I am refactoring the UI to the NextUI / HeroUI design system, replacing all SLA-related views.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Core Components**\\n\\nI\'m now defining the core components for the application\'s functionality. I\'m focusing on the product-affected column, CVE details, automated remediation steps, and notification history. I\'m building out components like a threat data view, advisories view, pipeline executions view, and alerted CVEs view. This will include threat feeds, recipients view, and audit logs.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"export type Severity = \'CRITICAL\' | \'HIGH\' | \'MEDIUM\' | \'LOW\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type ExposureLevel = \\\\n  | \'INTERNET_FACING\' \\\\n  | \'INTERNAL_CRITICAL\' \\\\n  | \'DMZ\' \\\\n  | \'WORKSTATION\' \\\\n  | \'CLOUD_INFRA\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type ExploitRiskLevel = \\\\n  | \'CISA_KEV_EXPLOITE\\n<truncated 5848 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Remove all SLA fields and introduce autonomous zero-touch exploit risk and auto-dispatch fields\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types/index.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating types\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Remove SLA from TypeScript types\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":70,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:01:23Z\",\"input_tokens\":4347,\"cache_read_tokens\":147437,\"output_tokens\":14537,\"thinking\":\"**Refocusing Product Tracking**\\n\\nI\'m currently revamping `src/data/seedData.ts`. The focus is shifting away from SLAs. Now, I\'m concentrating on autonomous, zero-human-intervention product tracking, specifically CISA KEV exploitation, along with CVSS/EPSS scoring. My goal is immediate, automated notification dispatch. I\'m also cleaning up the template, homing in on a technical Product Vulnerability Notification format.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import {\\\\n  ThreatFeed,\\\\n  WatchListItem,\\\\n  NormalizedCVE,\\\\n  Finding,\\\\n  Advisory,\\\\n  AlertedCVE,\\\\n  EmailRecipient,\\\\n  EmailDeliveryLog,\\\\n  AuditLog,\\\\n  AppSettings,\\\\n} from \'../types\';\\\\n\\\\nexport const INITIAL_FEEDS: ThreatFeed[] = [\\\\n  {\\\\n    id: \'fee\\n<truncated 38388 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update seedData removing all SLA references and setting autonomous product tracking data\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/data/seedData.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating seed data\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Clean seedData without SLA\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":72,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:02:41Z\",\"input_tokens\":15220,\"cache_read_tokens\":151311,\"output_tokens\":4100,\"thinking\":\"**Refactoring Core Logic**\\n\\nI\'m currently updating the `pipelineEngine.ts` file. I\'ve removed the SLA-related calculations, hours, tier escalations, and clock resets. Instead, I\'m integrating autonomous exploit risk assessment logic based on indicators like `CISA_KEV_EXPLOITED`, `WEAPONIZED_EXPLOIT`, and `HIGH_EPSS_PROBABILITY` to improve the response.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import {\\\\n  ThreatFeed,\\\\n  WatchListItem,\\\\n  NormalizedCVE,\\\\n  Finding,\\\\n  Advisory,\\\\n  AlertedCVE,\\\\n  PipelineExecution,\\\\n  PipelinePhase,\\\\n  AppSettings,\\\\n  ExploitRiskLevel,\\\\n  EmailDeliveryLog,\\\\n  AuditLog,\\\\n} from \'../types\';\\\\nimport { normalizeCveId\\n<truncated 13305 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update pipelineEngine removing SLA and enforcing zero-human-intervention auto-dispatch\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/engine/pipelineEngine.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating pipeline engine\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Remove SLA from pipeline engine\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":74,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:03:09Z\",\"input_tokens\":4383,\"cache_read_tokens\":166456,\"output_tokens\":6008,\"thinking\":\"**Refining AppContext Logic**\\n\\nI\'ve been working on refining `src/context/AppContext.tsx`. Specifically, I removed the SLA monitoring ticker. I\'m updating the findings status handlers, and I\'ve also removed SLA promotion and reset logic. Further, re-alerting is being adjusted to automatically dispatch a resend, and finally, I am also cleaning up the `AppContext` interface.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { createContext, useContext, useState, useEffect, useMemo, useCallback } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  ThreatFeed,\\\\n  WatchListItem,\\\\n  NormalizedCVE,\\\\n  Finding,\\\\n  Advisory,\\\\n  AlertedCVE,\\\\n  EmailRecipient,\\\\n  EmailDeliveryLog,\\\\n  AuditLog,\\\\\\n<truncated 20635 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update AppContext removing SLA ticker and adding zero-human-intervention auto-dispatch state\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/context/AppContext.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating AppContext\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Remove SLA from AppContext\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":76,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:03:44Z\",\"input_tokens\":6357,\"cache_read_tokens\":170688,\"output_tokens\":972,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing CSS Styling**\\n\\nI\'m currently reviewing `src/index.css` to align the styling with the requested professional, non-flashy UI for product vulnerability tracking. I\'m focusing on the React + NextUI UI, specifically aiming to eliminate any potentially problematic aspects while ensuring a clean, effective visual design free of an SLA. The goal is a UI that prioritizes clarity and a professional aesthetic over any distracting or \\\"flashy\\\" elements.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Refine index.css with NextUI zinc theme styling\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"28\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update base background and scrollbar colors to neutral zinc\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"@layer base {\\\\n  body {\\\\n    font-family: \'Plus Jakarta Sans\', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \\\\\\\"Segoe UI\\\\\\\", Roboto, sans-serif;\\\\n    background-color: #09090b;\\\\n    color: #f4f4f5;\\\\n    overflow-x: hidden;\\\\n  }\\\\n\\\\n  code, pre, .font-mono {\\\\n    font-f\\n<truncated 349 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"3\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"@layer base {\\\\n  body {\\\\n    font-family: \'Plus Jakarta Sans\', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \\\\\\\"Segoe UI\\\\\\\", Roboto, sans-serif;\\\\n    background-color: #0b0f17;\\\\n    color: #e2e8f0;\\\\n    overflow-x: hidden;\\\\n  }\\\\n\\\\n  cod