tes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update SettingsView with NextUI styling, removing SLA tiers and adding zero-human auto-dispatch settings\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating SettingsView\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update SettingsView to NextUI style without SLA\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":108,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:09:59Z\",\"input_tokens\":4397,\"cache_read_tokens\":234370,\"output_tokens\":1068,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { AppProvider, useApp } from \'./context/AppContext\';\\\\nimport { TopHeader } from \'./components/TopHeader\';\\\\nimport { DashboardView } from \'./components/DashboardView\';\\\\nimport { WatchListView } from \'./components/WatchLis\\n<truncated 3071 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update src/App.tsx with NextUI clean background and remove SLA from footer\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update App.tsx to NextUI style without SLA\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":110,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:10:09Z\",\"input_tokens\":3340,\"cache_read_tokens\":236606,\"output_tokens\":40,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":112,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:10:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":2250,\"cache_read_tokens\":237818,\"output_tokens\":62,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Linting applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Lint applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":114,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:10:20Z\",\"input_tokens\":2292,\"cache_read_tokens\":237939,\"output_tokens\":929,\"content\":\"### VulnStream \342\200\224 Autonomous Product Vulnerability Tracking & Notification System\\n\\nThe application has been completely redesigned with a **NextUI/HeroUI-inspired professional aesthetic**, all SLA constructs have been removed, and the platform has been tailored for **unattended product vulnerability tracking with zero human intervention**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Updates & Architectural Refinements\\n\\n1. **NextUI Design Language & Subtle Palette**\\n   - **Neutral Zinc Palette**: Replaced flashy, saturated neon colors wi\\n<truncated 1689 bytes>\\nline Scope Filtering ($O(1)$ canonical lookup)\\n     3. Multi-Source Auto-Enrichment (CVSS v3.1, EPSS probability, CISA KEV tags)\\n     4. Product Watch-List CPE 2.3 Matching\\n     5. Instant Automated Notification Dispatch (Mailgun TLS 1.3 / SMTP)\\n   - **Notification Ledger & Resend Capability**: Tracks all automatic transmissions in the delivery log and sent registry, with manual resend and exponential backoff retry support (`5m` $\\\\rightarrow$ `15m` $\\\\rightarrow$ `1h` $\\\\rightarrow$ `3h` $\\\\rightarrow$ `12h`).\",\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Project Requirements**\\n\\nOkay, both the `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` tasks are complete, with no reported errors, which is great news. I\'m now double-checking everything to ensure that the user\'s initial request is fully addressed. Specifically, I\'ve confirmed the \\\"React + NextUI UI\\\" requirement by adopting the NextUI/HeroUI design language, utilizing the neutral zinc-950/zinc-900 palettes.\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":115,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:13:43Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nsuggest imporvements\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T00:13:43-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-4bmuxvetm2tba5elubuyrh-950371923494.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-4bmuxvetm2tba5elubuyrh-950371923494.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: alamgir9@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":116,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:13:43Z\",\"input_tokens\":3277,\"cache_read_tokens\":238171,\"output_tokens\":1585,\"content\":\"Here are the most valuable enterprise improvements for **VulnStream**, focused on unattended product vulnerability tracking, zero-human-intervention notification, and the NextUI clean design system:\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. Multi-Channel Autonomous Webhook Routing (Slack, Teams, PagerDuty, Jira)\\n* **Current state**: Notifications are dispatched exclusively via email (Mailgun/SMTP).\\n* **Improvement**: Add an **Autonomous Notification Routing Matrix**:\\n  - **Inbound Webhook Destinations**: Route alerts directly to team c\\n<truncated 2740 bytes>\\nexamine the exact rendered payload before the live scheduler processes it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Which of these would you like to implement first?\\n1. **Multi-Channel Webhooks (Slack / Teams / PagerDuty / Webhook URL dispatch)**\\n2. **CPE Version Range Matching (SemVer comparison for zero false-positives)**\\n3. **Consolidated Digest Batching (prevents email flooding during multi-CVE releases)**\\n4. **SBOM Upload (CycloneDX / SPDX JSON import into product inventory)**\\n5. **Noise Reduction & Attack Vector Suppression Rules**\",\"thinking\":\"**Identifying Improvements**\\n\\nI\'m focusing on the current application state to suggest improvements. I\'m prioritizing realistic, high-value, enterprise-grade changes, starting with product vulnerabilities. My goal is to identify specific areas for enhancements.\\n\\n\\n**Prioritizing Enhancement Ideas**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on high-impact improvements, especially regarding autonomous dispatch and notification routing. My latest focus involves creating a flexible Autonomous Webhook & Notification Routing Matrix. Th\\n<truncated 287 bytes>\\nering capabilities. I\'m incorporating precise version range evaluation alongside CPE 2.3 matching to eliminate false positives on patched versions. Also, I\'m working on autonomous rules to suppress non-actionable alerts based on attack vector or EPSS scores, aiming to maintain clean notification inboxes and prevent alert fatigue. Lastly, I\'m building a Dry-Run Ingestion Tester to simulate CVEs and security bulletins, for distribution channel and message preview. I\'m also planning notification throttling.\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\",\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":117,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:15:50Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nsuggest improvements in matching and other core areas. sould be enterprise grade\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T00:15:50-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-4bmuxvetm2tba5elubuyrh-950371923494.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-4bmuxvetm2tba5elubuyrh-950371923494.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: alamgir9@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":118,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:15:50Z\",\"input_tokens\":3966,\"cache_read_tokens\":239513,\"output_tokens\":2573,\"content\":\"Here are the highest-impact, **enterprise-grade improvements** for **matching** and **core platform processing**, modeled after production platforms like Tenable, Wiz, and Snyk:\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. Enterprise Matching Engine Improvements\\n\\n#### A. NVD Version Interval & SemVer Predicate Matching\\n* **The Problem**: CPE 2.3 expressions without version range evaluation cause massive false positive rates (e.g., alerting on `pan-os:10.2.11` when the vulnerability was fixed in `10.2.4-h1`).\\n* **The Improvement**: Impleme\\n<truncated 4557 bytes>\\nications were dispatched with zero manual tampering or delay.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Suggested Next Step\\nWe can implement:\\n1. **The Advanced Version Interval Matcher** (`versionStart/End` predicate evaluation with SemVer/vendor build tag parser).\\n2. **Multi-Channel Signed Webhook Outbox** (Slack / Teams / Generic JSON Webhook with HMAC signature verification).\\n3. **The Anti-Flood Digest Batching Engine** (consolidates batch CVEs into single notifications).\\n\\nWhich of these would you like to build into the platform first?\",\"thinking\":\"**Considering Enterprise Upgrades**\\n\\nI\'m presently zeroing in on enterprise-level upgrades for matching, ingestion, correlation, and deduplication. Currently, I am focused on pinpointing architectural enhancements across these core areas, specifically with an eye toward improving scalability and reliability. The goal is to provide enterprise-grade solutions. I\'m exploring potential bottlenecks and considering alternative approaches to maximize performance.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing Core Processing**\\n\\nI\'m now delving in\\n<truncated 1165 bytes>\\nPrioritizing VEX**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on CSAF 2.0 with VEX. I\'m prioritizing `not_affected` and other VEX statements to suppress false alarms, implementing immediate suppression based on vendor markings like \\\"component not present.\\\" I\'m also grappling with cross-source conflicts, establishing configurable authority precedence to resolve discrepancies between NVD and vendor PSIRTs, where vendor PSIRT is prioritized. Furthermore, I\'m working to implement content-addressable hashing to optimize ingestion.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\",\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":119,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:17:37Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nimplement all\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T00:17:37-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-4bmuxvetm2tba5elubuyrh-950371923494.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-4bmuxvetm2tba5elubuyrh-950371923494.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: alamgir9@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":120,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:17:37Z\",\"input_tokens\":246674,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1669,\"thinking\":\"**Implementing the Plan**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on implementing the advanced NVD version interval and SemVer matching engine. Specifically, I\'m working on the granular interval options like `versionStartIncluding`, `versionStartExcluding`, `versionEndIncluding`, and `versionEndExcluding`. I\'m starting with the SemVer logic.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding the Features**\\n\\nI\'m now integrating vendor build tag comparison for nuanced versioning (e.g., `11.0.4-h1`). PURL and dual identifier evaluation are being added for comprehensive\\n<truncated 693 bytes>\\nAudit System**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the anti-flood measures for the webhooks, adding batching settings and implementing cryptographic audit hash chain fields to maintain data integrity. I\'m also working to implement an enterprise-grade SemVer and vendor build tag interval checker. I\'m expanding CPE matching by integrating version interval criteria, architecture filtering, and PURL matching, and improving vendor/product matching. Finally, I\'m integrating the various components in the pipeline engine.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * Cryptographic Utility for Tamper-Evident Audit Hash Chains and Webhook HMAC Signatures\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\n// Simple robust browser-compatible SHA-256 implementation\\\\nexport async function sha256(message: string): Promise<string> {\\\\n  const msgUint8 = new Tex\\n<truncated 990 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create cryptoChain utility for audit hash chain and webhook HMAC signatures\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/utils/cryptoChain.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating cryptoChain.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create cryptographic audit and HMAC utility\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":122,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:17:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":3976,\"cache_read_tokens\":244844,\"output_tokens\":1398,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Version Comparator**\\n\\nI\'m now building `src/utils/versionComparator.ts`. My focus is on robust version comparison, covering enterprise SemVer, vendor build tags, and NVD version interval evaluation. I\'m aiming for accuracy when comparing versions with formats like `10.2.3`, `10.2.4-h1`, or `6.1.0-21-amd64`, including evaluating `versionStartIncluding` and `versionStart`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * Enterprise Version Range & SemVer Comparator\\\\n * Evaluates NVD Version Match Criteria intervals [versionStart, versionEnd)\\\\n * Handles standard SemVer, Linux kernels, and vendor patch tags (e.g. 11.0.4-h1, 7.4.3.F-build2573).\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nexport interf\\n<truncated 3630 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create versionComparator utility for enterprise NVD version intervals and SemVer matching\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/utils/versionComparator.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating versionComparator.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create SemVer and NVD range comparator\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":124,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:18:07Z\",\"input_tokens\":3697,\"cache_read_tokens\":246740,\"output_tokens\":2550,\"thinking\":\"**Expanding Matching Capabilities**\\n\\nI\'m currently working to expand `src/utils/cpeMatcher.ts`. I\'m integrating support for NVD version interval criteria using `versionRange?`, PURL matching with the `purl?` field, and target architecture validation via `target_hw`. Furthermore, I\'m implementing boolean configuration matching with the `operator?` field, allowing for both \'AND\' and \'OR\' logic.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * Enterprise CPE 2.3 Strict Component Matcher, SemVer Range Evaluator & PURL Matcher\\\\n * Spec: NIST IR 7695 & Package URL (purl-spec)\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nimport { NvdVersionRange, isVersionInNvdRange } from \'./versionComparator\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface ParsedCPE {\\n<truncated 7657 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Enhance cpeMatcher with NVD version range criteria, PURL support, and architecture token evaluation\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/utils/cpeMatcher.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating cpeMatcher.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update CPE matcher with version intervals and PURL\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":126,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:18:24Z\",\"input_tokens\":2768,\"cache_read_tokens\":250427,\"output_tokens\":2753,\"thinking\":\"**Updating Type Definitions**\\n\\nI\'m currently updating the type definitions in `src/types/index.ts`. I\'ve added `NvdVersionRange` to `NormalizedCVE`. Also, I\'ve integrated the `purl` field into both `WatchListItem` and `NormalizedCVE`. Finally, I\'ve incorporated the VEX statement with a `vexStatus` field, including \'affected\', \'not_affected\', and \'fixed\' options.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import { NvdVersionRange } from \'../utils/versionComparator\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type Severity = \'CRITICAL\' | \'HIGH\' | \'MEDIUM\' | \'LOW\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type ExposureLevel = \\\\n  | \'INTERNET_FACING\' \\\\n  | \'INTERNAL_CRITICAL\' \\\\n  | \'DMZ\' \\\\n  | \'WORKSTATION\' \\\\n  | \'CLOUD_I\\n<truncated 7250 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update types with version intervals, PURL, VEX, Webhook outbox, and cryptographic audit hash chain\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types/index.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating types\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add enterprise types for version intervals, VEX, webhooks, and audit chain\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":128,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:18:41Z\",\"input_tokens\":2976,\"cache_read_tokens\":253181,\"output_tokens\":11723,\"thinking\":\"**Adding Seed Data Details**\\n\\nI\'m now integrating `versionRange` and `vex` examples into normalized CVEs within `src/data/seedData.ts`. Specifically, I\'m working with examples like `CVE-2024-3400`, defining the `versionRange` with details such as `versionStartIncluding` and `versionEndExcluding` for a more comprehensive representation.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import {\\\\n  ThreatFeed,\\\\n  WatchListItem,\\\\n  NormalizedCVE,\\\\n  Finding,\\\\n  Advisory,\\\\n  AlertedCVE,\\\\n  EmailRecipient,\\\\n  EmailDeliveryLog,\\\\n  AuditLog,\\\\n  AppSettings,\\\\n  WebhookEndpoint,\\\\n  WebhookDeliveryLog,\\\\n} from \'../types\';\\\\nimport { quickHash } f\\n<truncated 29276 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Seed enterprise data including version intervals, VEX suppression demo, webhooks, and tamper-evident audit hash chain\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/data/seedData.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating seedData.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update seed data for enterprise features\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}"
