  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Eliminating SLA References**\n\nI\'ve just confirmed the complete removal of all \"SLA\" mentions, thankfully, only \"SLACK\" was found! The codebase is now clean. The next step will be working on the UI. The application will track product vulnerabilities and send notifications, and will be automated, so the UI needs to reflect that.\n\n\n**Refining Enterprise Design**\n\nI\'m now focusing on enterprise-grade improvements. I need to make the application world-class for production use and deeply automated. My thoughts have landed on interactive autonomous pipeline simulation and inspection. This includes an Autonomous Operations Center to visualize the automated processes, including a chronological cron timer and an auto-dispatch rule engine. This should enhance vulnerability tracking and notifications.\n\n\n**Enhancing Matching Engine**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the Matching Engine improvements. My focus is on achieving best-in-class enterprise vulnerability matching. I\'m prioritizing comprehensive CPE parsing and validation (both 2.3 and 2.2 formats), alongside robust SemVer range comparisons, including multi-interval evaluation, wildcard handling, and pre-release/build metadata support. Furthermore, I\'m integrating native support for Package URLs (PURLs), which will enable modern container and SBOM compatibility. I will be incorporating Zero-Touch Notification Dispatch logs showing exactly what was dispatched autonomously with NO human approval button needed!\n\n\n**Developing Matching Refinements**\n\nI\'m expanding the matching engine further. My focus now includes a vendor and product synonym dictionary to normalize aliases such as `f5` to `f5_networks`. I\'m also implementing contextual environmental exclusion rules for de-noising, considering hardware architecture and VEX CSAF 2.0 evaluations. Finally, I\'m excited about developing an interactive matching playground/simulator, enabling security teams to test any CPE or PURL strings against current CVEs.\n\n\n**Visualizing Match Evaluations**\n\nI\'m now detailing a feature showing real-time match evaluation traces, which will include a step-by-step breakdown (Vendor, Product, Version, Context, Exploitability). I believe this is a critical enterprise-level feature, very exciting for SOC and DevSecOps teams!\n\n\n"
