  planner_response {
    response: "### Summary of Implemented Enterprise Capabilities\n\nThe application has been upgraded into an autonomous, enterprise-grade product vulnerability intelligence and automated notification system, built with a refined NextUI-inspired dark interface (`zinc`/`slate` theme, crisp monospace identifiers, subtle borders, and zero flashy or distracting colors). All SLA tracking logic has been replaced with autonomous zero-touch dispatch routing, product blast radius, exploit likelihood, and de-noising controls.\n\n---\n\n### Key Improvements & Architecture\n\n#### 1. Enterprise-Grade Matching Engine (CPE-First + PURL + SemVer Intervals)\n* **Strict NIST CPE 2.3 & 2.2 Dual Parsing:** Well-Formed Name (WFN) tokenization across Part (`a`, `o`, `h`), Vendor, Product, Version, Edition, Target SW, and Target HW (`/src/utils/cpeMatcher.ts`).\n* **Semantic Version & Interval Evaluation:** Correlates asset installed versions with explicit NVD interval bounds (`versionStartIncluding`, `versionEndExcluding`, `versionEndIncluding`, wildcard minor/patch `10.2.x`, pre-releases).\n* **Package URL (PURL) Resolution:** Native SBOM & dependency matching (`pkg:npm/...`, `pkg:maven/...`, `pkg:pypi/...`, `pkg:golang/...`, `pkg:cargo/...`).\n* **Vendor & Product Synonym Thesaurus:** Normalizes vendor/product aliases automatically (e.g., `paloaltonetworks` \342\206\224 `palo alto` / `panw`, `f5` \342\206\224 `f5_networks`, `msft` \342\206\224 `microsoft`, `apache` \342\206\224 `httpd`, `k8s` \342\206\224 `kubernetes`).\n* **Contextual De-Noising & Target Architecture Filter:** Verifies Target Hardware (`x86_64`, `aarch64`) and Target OS (`linux`, `windows`) to eliminate out-of-context matches.\n* **CSAF 2.0 VEX Exploitability Gate:** Automatically flags and suppresses findings where the vendor has published a verified `not_affected` statement (e.g., vulnerable code path disabled or uncompiled), preventing alarm fatigue.\n* **Confidence Scoring & Explanatory Trace:** Computes match confidence (100% Strict CPE Interval, 95% PURL Exact, 85% Alias Thesaurus, 70% Heuristic Fallback) with evidence logs.\n\n#### 2. Interactive Matching Simulator & Rule Lab\n* Located directly within **Monitored Products (`WatchListView`)**:\n  * **Testing Presets:** Instant evaluation for Palo Alto PAN-OS 10.2, Apache HTTP Server 2.4.49, Fortinet FortiOS 7.2.4, Cisco IOS XE 17.9.4, and Log4j-Core PURL 2.14.1.\n  * **Evaluation Engine:** Step-by-step breakdown (Identifier Tokenization \342\206\222 Alias Resolution \342\206\222 SemVer Interval Evaluation \342\206\222 Architecture De-Noiser \342\206\222 VEX Gate \342\206\222 Autonomous Routing).\n\n#### 3. Autonomous Multi-Channel Dispatch (Zero Human Intervention)\n* **Rule-Based Autonomous Dispatch:**\n  * `CRITICAL` / `CISA_KEV` / `EPSS \342\211\245 0.40` \342\206\222 **Immediate Emergency Notification** (Slack Webhook + High-Priority Email).\n  * `MEDIUM` / `LOW` \342\206\222 **Scheduled Digest Batch**.\n  * `VEX not_affected` \342\206\222 **Suppressed with Cryptographic Audit Trail**.\n* **Autonomous Webhook Channels (`RecipientsView`):**\n  * Configurable webhooks for **Slack Incoming Webhooks**, **Microsoft Teams**, and **Enterprise SIEM / SOAR (HMAC-SHA256)**.\n  * Live test dispatch modal with simulated `X-VulnStream-Signature-256` payload verification.\n* **Deduplication & Re-Alerting:** Canonical `CVE-YYYY-NNNN+` normalization, in-run duplicate suppression, and automated re-alerting triggers upon threat escalation."
    thinking: "**Verifying System Status**\n\nOkay, I\'ve confirmed the SLA purge, with no lingering references detected \342\200\223 just Slack mentions. The autonomous vulnerability tracking is solid; the system ingests multiple feeds and employs CPE 2.3 for stringent component matching.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Summary of Implemented Enterprise Capabilities\n\nThe application has been upgraded into an autonomous, enterprise-grade product vulnerability intelligence and automated notification system, built with a refined NextUI-inspired dark interface (`zinc`/`slate` theme, crisp monospace identifiers, subtle borders, and zero flashy or distracting colors). All SLA tracking logic has been replaced with autonomous zero-touch dispatch routing, product blast radius, exploit likelihood, and de-noising controls.\n\n---\n\n### Key Improvements & Architecture\n\n#### 1. Enterprise-Grade Matching Engine (CPE-First + PURL + SemVer Intervals)\n* **Strict NIST CPE 2.3 & 2.2 Dual Parsing:** Well-Formed Name (WFN) tokenization across Part (`a`, `o`, `h`), Vendor, Product, Version, Edition, Target SW, and Target HW (`/src/utils/cpeMatcher.ts`).\n* **Semantic Version & Interval Evaluation:** Correlates asset installed versions with explicit NVD interval bounds (`versionStartIncluding`, `versionEndExcluding`, `versionEndIncluding`, wildcard minor/patch `10.2.x`, pre-releases).\n* **Package URL (PURL) Resolution:** Native SBOM & dependency matching (`pkg:npm/...`, `pkg:maven/...`, `pkg:pypi/...`, `pkg:golang/...`, `pkg:cargo/...`).\n* **Vendor & Product Synonym Thesaurus:** Normalizes vendor/product aliases automatically (e.g., `paloaltonetworks` \342\206\224 `palo alto` / `panw`, `f5` \342\206\224 `f5_networks`, `msft` \342\206\224 `microsoft`, `apache` \342\206\224 `httpd`, `k8s` \342\206\224 `kubernetes`).\n* **Contextual De-Noising & Target Architecture Filter:** Verifies Target Hardware (`x86_64`, `aarch64`) and Target OS (`linux`, `windows`) to eliminate out-of-context matches.\n* **CSAF 2.0 VEX Exploitability Gate:** Automatically flags and suppresses findings where the vendor has published a verified `not_affected` statement (e.g., vulnerable code path disabled or uncompiled), preventing alarm fatigue.\n* **Confidence Scoring & Explanatory Trace:** Computes match confidence (100% Strict CPE Interval, 95% PURL Exact, 85% Alias Thesaurus, 70% Heuristic Fallback) with evidence logs.\n\n#### 2. Interactive Matching Simulator & Rule Lab\n* Located directly within **Monitored Products (`WatchListView`)**:\n  * **Testing Presets:** Instant evaluation for Palo Alto PAN-OS 10.2, Apache HTTP Server 2.4.49, Fortinet FortiOS 7.2.4, Cisco IOS XE 17.9.4, and Log4j-Core PURL 2.14.1.\n  * **Evaluation Engine:** Step-by-step breakdown (Identifier Tokenization \342\206\222 Alias Resolution \342\206\222 SemVer Interval Evaluation \342\206\222 Architecture De-Noiser \342\206\222 VEX Gate \342\206\222 Autonomous Routing).\n\n#### 3. Autonomous Multi-Channel Dispatch (Zero Human Intervention)\n* **Rule-Based Autonomous Dispatch:**\n  * `CRITICAL` / `CISA_KEV` / `EPSS \342\211\245 0.40` \342\206\222 **Immediate Emergency Notification** (Slack Webhook + High-Priority Email).\n  * `MEDIUM` / `LOW` \342\206\222 **Scheduled Digest Batch**.\n  * `VEX not_affected` \342\206\222 **Suppressed with Cryptographic Audit Trail**.\n* **Autonomous Webhook Channels (`RecipientsView`):**\n  * Configurable webhooks for **Slack Incoming Webhooks**, **Microsoft Teams**, and **Enterprise SIEM / SOAR (HMAC-SHA256)**.\n  * Live test dispatch modal with simulated `X-VulnStream-Signature-256` payload verification.\n* **Deduplication & Re-Alerting:** Canonical `CVE-YYYY-NNNN+` normalization, in-run duplicate suppression, and automated re-alerting triggers upon threat escalation."
