  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Intent**\n\nI am now focusing on the user\'s specific request concerning the email template. I need to eliminate the HTML Email Template box and directly enable modifications on the Rendered Client Preview. The required options include font color, font style adjustments, and the addition of drawing objects and other changes. I am evaluating how to achieve this functionality most effectively.\n\n\n**Refining Template Design**\n\nI\'m now implementing the latest updates. I have eliminated the HTML email template box, and renamed \"Rendered Client Preview\" to \"HTML template.\" My next step is to enable direct modifications on the \"HTML template.\" This will include intuitive controls like font family adjustments (Sans-Serif, Modern Monospace, Serif, Clean System), font weight, size scale, and a primary text color picker. I am working to make these changes directly manipulatable.\n\n\n**Expanding Color Options**\n\nI am now focusing on expanding the available color customization. I\'ve added options for heading color, accent/link color, and muted caption color. I\'m also implementing color options for the background: Email Canvas, Content Card, and Header banner, including pre-set and custom hex color choices. I\'ve started the implementation of visual stamps and drawing object additions.\n\n\n**Implementing Global Style Application**\n\nI am now focusing on applying user customizations globally. When a user customizes and saves the styles, I need to update `advisoryTemplate` within `AppContext`. This includes all subsequent pipeline-generated advisories, new notifications, and test emails. This involves applying font colors, backgrounds, styles, and stamps. Now, I am turning my attention to a UI redesign, so I can start to tackle the menu.\n\n\n**Adding Theme Toggles**\n\nI\'m now integrating dark and light mode support within the application. I have added `theme: \'dark\' | \'light\'` and `toggleTheme()` to `AppContext`. I am incorporating the necessary CSS classes for dark and light mode styles in `src/index.css`. This includes implementing a toggle in both the top header and sidebar bottom, using Sun/Moon icons, to allow users to switch between themes.\n\n**Refining CVE Filtering**\n\nI\'m currently refining the CVE filtering logic within `src/engine/pipelineEngine.ts`. I\'m ensuring `isWithinTimelineScope` now strictly checks both `cve.publishedDate` and `cve.modifiedDate`, in addition to the other filtering criteria. I will also make sure the log message clearly indicates filtering by both dates.\n\n\n**Implementing Pagination**\n\nI\'m now implementing the pagination controls. I am working on creating the reusable `Pagination` component and I\'m adding pagination to several views, including findings, watchlist, threat data, and threat feeds. I also plan to add pagination to the email history, operational logs, and alerted CVEs views.\n\n\n"
