    session_summary: "{\"step_index\":131,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:19:47Z\",\"input_tokens\":13661,\"cache_read_tokens\":18468,\"output_tokens\":512,\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Compilation Status**\\n\\nI\'m currently checking the build status by running `compile_applet`. Before that, I needed to check if this is a new task or a prompt shift. The prompt itself is under consideration.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing User Requests**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s explicit directives, especially regarding the removal of SLA features. The prompt highlights a need for a professional UI, with the removal of flashy elements. This is a very specific direction to improve the product matching, which I am actively considering for optimization. The user also wants enterprise-grade quality.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking app compilation\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":133,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:19:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":2653,\"cache_read_tokens\":30195,\"output_tokens\":1104,\"thinking\":\"**Inspecting The Build**\\n\\nI\'ve got a successful build, so I\'m now meticulously examining the files. My primary focus is on removing the Service Level Agreement (SLA) completely. The user\'s directive is clear: eliminate it, as this application tracks product vulnerabilities and sends automated notifications. I\'m prioritizing this refactor to ensure it aligns with the user\'s specific request.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Application Autonomy**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on the application\'s autonomous capabilities. The goal is to e\\n<truncated 1253 bytes>\\nbased matches with version heuristics at 70%. Each match will include a trace, showing the rule or CPE/PURL that triggered it.\\n\\nI\'m now integrating an autonomous de-noising and false-positive suppression engine. This will use architecture/OS filtering and component status to suppress false positives. I\'m also including known false-positive suppression rules with audit logging. The focus is on a clean, professional user interface, inspired by NextUI, using dark enterprise themes with zinc and slate tones.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"list_dir\",\"args\":{\"DirectoryPath\":\"\\\"/src\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Listing src directory\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"List src contents\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":135,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:20:08Z\",\"input_tokens\":3345,\"cache_read_tokens\":31210,\"output_tokens\":81,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"list_dir\",\"args\":{\"DirectoryPath\":\"\\\"/src/components\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Listing components directory\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"List components\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":137,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:20:10Z\",\"input_tokens\":2403,\"cache_read_tokens\":32465,\"output_tokens\":63,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/types/index.ts\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading src/types/index.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View types\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":139,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:20:14Z\",\"input_tokens\":3889,\"cache_read_tokens\":34816,\"output_tokens\":178,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Type Definitions**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining `src/types/index.ts`. It\'s great that I\'ve found no Service Level Agreement (SLA) references there, and I noted the presence of types like `ExploitRiskLevel` (lines 12-17) and `NotificationStatus` (lines 19-26), which seems promising. The `NotificationStatus` enum, in particular, with states like `AUTO_DISPATCHED`, `QUEUED_FOR_DISPATCH`, etc., is helpful.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/utils/cpeMatcher.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"120\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking cpeMatcher.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View cpeMatcher\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":141,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:20:18Z\",\"input_tokens\":3858,\"cache_read_tokens\":36711,\"output_tokens\":107,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View App.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":143,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:20:22Z\",\"input_tokens\":3555,\"cache_read_tokens\":38465,\"output_tokens\":81,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/TopHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing TopHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View TopHeader\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":145,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:20:26Z\",\"input_tokens\":3859,\"cache_read_tokens\":39916,\"output_tokens\":940,\"thinking\":\"**Verifying System Autonomy**\\n\\nI\'m checking all the views and components. I need to make sure there are absolutely no mentions of Service Level Agreements anywhere. The goal is complete autonomy. This refactoring is crucial!\\n\\n\\n**Refining Aesthetic Consistency**\\n\\nI\'m now fully immersed in the UI consistency. Ensuring NextUI aesthetic is uniform is paramount, inspecting components like `DashboardView`, `FindingsView`, and more. I am focusing on dark card surfaces, crisp tabs, clean badges, and elegant typography for the UI. No neon colors!\\n\\n\\n**Developing Autonomous Alerting**\\n\\nI\'m now deeply engaged in the autonomous alerting pipeline. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the automated risk scoring, combining different factors like CVSS, EPSS, CISA KEV data, and asset exposure to prioritize alerts. The goal is zero human intervention; I am setting up a multi-channel autonomous dispatch system for immediate alerts.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/DashboardView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking DashboardView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View DashboardView\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":147,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:20:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":2743,\"cache_read_tokens\":43916,\"output_tokens\":84,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/FindingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking FindingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View FindingsView\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":149,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:20:42Z\",\"input_tokens\":3562,\"cache_read_tokens\":44549,\"output_tokens\":141,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"60\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View SettingsView\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":151,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:20:46Z\",\"input_tokens\":3174,\"cache_read_tokens\":46008,\"output_tokens\":112,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"grep -rn -i \\\\\\\"sla\\\\\\\" src/\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"2000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Searching for SLA in src\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Search for SLA occurrences\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":153,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:20:50Z\",\"input_tokens\":2648,\"cache_read_tokens\":47087,\"output_tokens\":1382,\"thinking\":\"**Eliminating SLA References**\\n\\nI\'ve just confirmed the complete removal of all \\\"SLA\\\" mentions, thankfully, only \\\"SLACK\\\" was found! The codebase is now clean. The next step will be working on the UI. The application will track product vulnerabilities and send notifications, and will be automated, so the UI needs to reflect that.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Enterprise Design**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on enterprise-grade improvements. I need to make the application world-class for production use and deeply automated. My thoughts \\n<truncated 1255 bytes>\\ne architecture and VEX CSAF 2.0 evaluations. Finally, I\'m excited about developing an interactive matching playground/simulator, enabling security teams to test any CPE or PURL strings against current CVEs.\\n\\n\\n**Visualizing Match Evaluations**\\n\\nI\'m now detailing a feature showing real-time match evaluation traces, which will include a step-by-step breakdown (Vendor, Product, Version, Context, Exploitability). I believe this is a critical enterprise-level feature, very exciting for SOC and DevSecOps teams!\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/WatchListView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking WatchListView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View WatchListView\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":155,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:21:04Z\",\"input_tokens\":2877,\"cache_read_tokens\":50117,\"output_tokens\":96,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/TopHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"227\",\"StartLine\":\"100\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking navigation tabs in TopHeader.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View TopHeader navigation tabs\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":157,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:21:08Z\",\"input_tokens\":2558,\"cache_read_tokens\":52934,\"output_tokens\":105,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/WatchListView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"250\",\"StartLine\":\"150\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing WatchListView tabs and features\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View WatchListView body\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":159,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:21:11Z\",\"input_tokens\":4155,\"cache_read_tokens\":53354,\"output_tokens\":1245,\"thinking\":\"**Envisioning Enterprise Matching**\\n\\nI\'m now picturing an \\\"Enterprise Matching Inspector & Simulator\\\" as a tab or drawer within `WatchListView.tsx`, or perhaps as a standalone tool! I\'m leaning towards the former as it seems more streamlined. The user\'s directive is driving this design, and it\342\200\231s become clear that enterprise-grade enhancements are crucial for matching improvements and other core areas. I\'m focusing on the implementation!\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing Matching Requirements**\\n\\nI\'m deep-diving into the speci\\n<truncated 699 bytes>\\nusing on the integration of this interactive \\\"Engine Lab\\\" and the \\\"Autonomous Alerting & Notification\\\" flow.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Alert Dispatches**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on automating alert dispatches. This includes role-based email filtering (CISA, critical, all severities), webhook integrations with Slack, Teams, and SIEM/SOAR systems. I\'m prioritizing batching low-severity alerts into digests and de-noising the output through CVE-ID normalization and duplicate suppression. The goal is to avoid alert fatigue!\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/data/seedData.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"120\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking seedData.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View seedData\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":161,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:21:26Z\",\"input_tokens\":3221,\"cache_read_tokens\":57773,\"output_tokens\":550,\"thinking\":\"**Examining Matching Simulator**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on enhancing the `WatchListView.tsx` component. My primary aim is to integrate a \\\"Enterprise Matching Engine & Simulator.\\\" I envision this as a dedicated tab or modal allowing users to test products, CPE 2.3 strings, and PURLs against the matching engine.\\n\\n\\n**Developing Matching Engine Logic**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the core logic of the matching engine. I\'m breaking down the evaluation process into discrete, observable steps. I\'m starting with CPE token parsing and PURL component resolution, and moving into alias lookups and SemVer version comparisons against NVD and feed data. I\'m also planning to incorporate architecture and target OS de-noising and VEX exploitability assessment. Finally, I\'m considering a calculated confidence score and autonomous notification actions.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/RecipientsView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking RecipientsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View RecipientsView\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":163,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:21:32Z\",\"input_tokens\":2143,\"cache_read_tokens\":61103,\"output_tokens\":89,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/context/AppContext.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"140\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking AppContext.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View AppContext interface\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":165,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:21:37Z\",\"input_tokens\":2402,\"cache_read_tokens\":63178,\"output_tokens\":99,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/engine/pipelineEngine.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"150\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking pipelineEngine.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View pipelineEngine\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":167,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:21:41Z\",\"input_tokens\":2406,\"cache_read_tokens\":65514,\"output_tokens\":97,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/engine/pipelineEngine.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"380\",\"StartLine\":\"151\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking pipelineEngine.ts phases 3-5\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View pipelineEngine matching and dispatch\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":169,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:21:44Z\",\"input_tokens\":3680,\"cache_read_tokens\":67830,\"output_tokens\":1612,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Pipeline Stats**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the `stats` object within `pipelineEngine.ts`, specifically at line 358. My primary interest lies in understanding the data flow within this object, particularly the relationship between `rawIngested`, `normalized`, and `deduplicated` metrics. I\'m trying to decipher how these stats reflect data processing at various stages. I\'m exploring how these values change as a function of the total inputs. I have a working hypothesis, but I am still building confi\\n<truncated 1567 bytes>\\ne webhook channels, considering Slack, Microsoft Teams, and generic SIEM/SOAR integration with HMAC-SHA256 verification. I\'m focusing on the ability to test webhook delivery instantly, including simulated payloads, signature generation, and response verification. I\'m also examining the VEX engine\'s role in suppressing alerts based on declarations and how this is visualized with a specific filter and badge. Finally, I\'m analyzing the autonomous decision matrix within the display views for rule evaluation.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/WatchListView.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"300\",\"StartLine\":\"200\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing WatchListView layout\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View WatchListView mid section\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":171,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:21:59Z\",\"input_tokens\":3852,\"cache_read_tokens\":71942,\"output_tokens\":659,\"thinking\":\"**Exploring Integration Design**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on integrating a new feature, specifically an \\\"Enterprise Matching Engine & Simulator,\\\" directly into `WatchListView.tsx`. The design\'s starting to take shape; I\'m picturing a switcher at the top to toggle between the existing \\\"Monitored Products Inventory\\\" view and the new tool, allowing users to select `[ Monitored Products Inventory (8) ]` as one option. This should streamline workflow.\\n\\n\\n**Testing Simulator Functionality**\\n\\nI\'m now putting the \\\"Enterprise Matching Engine & Simulator\\\" through its paces. I\'m focusing on defining input parameters \342\200\223 Vendor, Product, Version, and optional CPE 2.3 string, PURL, target architecture/OS, and VEX Status. The plan is to click \\\"Simulate Matching & Evaluate Rules\\\" to run against the normalized CVE corpus, and show detailed evaluation steps, starting with canonical identifier parsing and alias resolution.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/utils/cpeMatcher.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"250\",\"StartLine\":\"121\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking rest of cpeMatcher.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View cpeMatcher logic\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":173,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T07:22:06Z\",\"input_tokens\":2923,\"cache_read_tokens\":75894,\"output_tokens\":5389,\"thinking\":\"**Examining Matching Enhancements**\\n\\nI\'ve got a good base going with `cpeMatcher.ts`. Now, I\'m focusing on enterprise-level improvements for matching within `src/utils/cpeMatcher.ts`. I\'m starting by researching a good alias/synonym thesaurus because of the varying naming conventions used across different data sources like advisories, NVD, and GHSA.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Alias Relationships**\\n\\nI\'m now mapping out alias relationships for common vendors and products. I\'ve compiled a list of synonyms for internal asset\\n<truncated 678 bytes>\\ndence, as well as a count of suppressed CVEs. Finally, I\'ll integrate the Enterprise Matching Simulator into `WatchListView.tsx`.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding Autonomous Features**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on adding new features related to autonomous functionality. In `RecipientsView.tsx`, I\'ll integrate an \\\"Autonomous Webhooks\\\" tab for enhanced integration. In `DashboardView.tsx`, I am planning a visual summary for the autonomous engine. In `FindingsView.tsx`, I plan to ensure evidence and status are displayed in the drawer.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Enhance cpeMatcher with alias thesaurus, confidence scoring, contextual de-noising, and simulator helper\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"250\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add alias thesaurus, confidence score, architecture de-noising, and simulateProductMatch function\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"  const asset = parseCPE23(assetCpeStr);\\\\n  const vuln = parseCPE23(vulnCpeStr);\\\\n\\\\n  if (!asset.isValid || !vuln.isValid) {\\\\n    return { matched: false, reason: \'Invalid CPE syntax\' };\\\\n  }\\\\n\\\\n  // Part match (application, os, hardware)\\\\n  if (!matchCom\\n<truncated 8866 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"121\",\"Target