    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "build a modern application, enterprise grade Multi-source feed ingestion \342\200\224 normalizes and deduplicates CVEs from NVD, OpenCVE, CISA KEV, GHSA, OSV, VulCheck, and EPSS enrichment data into a unified record format.\n\nConfigurable threat feed management \342\200\224 admins can add/edit/delete custom RSS/Atom, STIX 2.x, TAXII 2.1, GitHub Advisory, and JSON Search API feed sources with per-feed auth (API key, bearer, basic) and rate limiting. Includes 16 pre-seeded vendor feeds (Microsoft, Fortinet, Cisco, VMware, Adobe, etc.).\n\nWatch-list matching (CPE-first) \342\200\224 strict CPE 2.3 component matching with vendor/product fallback. Supports multi-CPE entries per watch-list item with auto-resolution from NVD.\n\nTimeline scope filtering \342\200\224 configurable scope_hours (default 24h); checks published/modified dates against the processing window.\n\nDeduplication \342\200\224 canonical CVE ID normalization (uppercase, trimmed); O(1) lookup against previously-alerted CVEs and in-run duplicates.\n\nAuto-enrichment \342\200\224 NVD batch data fills missing CVSS scores, descriptions, CPEs, and dates for KEV entries before classification.\n\nPriority classification \342\200\224 CISA KEV (6h SLA), EPSS > 0.40, active exploits, and CVSS thresholds (9.0+/7.0+/4.0+) with internet-facing escalation.\n\nRemediation generation \342\200\224 vendor-specific patch URLs, immediate actions, workarounds, rollback plans, and step-by-step remediation instructions per CVE.\n\nSLA tracking \342\200\224 per-finding SLA deadlines (CISA KEV: 6h, Critical: 24h, High: 72h, Medium: 168h) with breach detection and clock-reset on tier promotions.\n\nWeb\nDashboard \342\200\224 vulnerability statistics, exposure summary, recent pipeline activity.\n\nWatch List \342\200\224 manage vendor/product/CPE assets with exposure classification and bulk JSON import (max 1000 entries).\n\nAlerted CVEs \342\200\224 track CVEs already sent to recipients; supports re-alerting after remediation.\n\nThreat Data \342\200\224 inspect normalized threat intelligence in the feed cache.\n\nAdvisories \342\200\224 review generated advisories with delivery status, affected CVEs, and PDF export (WeasyPrint/ReportLab fallback).\n\nFindings \342\200\224 triage, filter, and prioritize actionable vulnerabilities with remediation workflow.\n\nPipeline Executions \342\200\224 live execution flow with phase-by-phase progress (fetch feeds \342\206\222 enrich \342\206\222 classify \342\206\222 persist report \342\206\222 deliver notifications).\n\nReports \342\200\224 download pipeline output as JSON with full advisory details.\n\nEmail History \342\200\224 notification delivery attempts with provider status and retry tracking.\n\nThreat Feeds \342\200\224 enable/disable, test connectivity, and monitor health of feed sources.\n\nRecipients \342\200\224 manage the security distribution list with email validation.\n\nAdvisory Template \342\200\224 editable HTML email template with live preview and test-send to a configured recipient.\n\nSettings \342\200\224 database config, scheduler/NTP tuning, email (Mailgun) config, timezone/date format, advisory number prefix.\n\nUser Profile \342\200\224 password changes (12+ char minimum), account preferences.\n\nOperational Logs \342\200\224 searchable audit trail of system, pipeline, email, and security events.\n\nSecurity\nCSRF tokens on all state-changing requests (constant-time comparison)\n30-min session timeout with HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure cookies (production)\nSecurity headers: CSP, X-Frame-Options DENY, X-Content-Type-Options nosniff, HSTS, Permissions-Policy, COOP/CORP\nSSRF protection on feed URLs (rejects private/loopback/link-local addresses, no credential/redirect following)\nFeed API keys encrypted at rest (Werkzeug PBKDF2), never stored in config_json\nNo default credentials \342\200\224 users provisioned through controlled bootstrap\nInput validation: CVE ID format, email regex, CPE 2.3 format, bounded integer fields\nHTML output escaping on all feed-derived data\nDatabase-backed login rate limiting (5 attempts / 15-min lockout) with audit logging\nDatabase advisory lock on migrations; schema-staleness enforcement at startup\nPostgreSQL bind to 127.0.0.1 by default; configurable bind address\nAutonomous Operation\nBackground scheduler \342\200\224 APScheduler runs the full pipeline at configurable intervals (default 60 min) with max_instances=1 and self-healing for stale jobs.\n\nRetry with backoff \342\200\224 pipeline failures retry at 1/5/15 min; email delivery retries at 5 min / 15 min / 1h / 3h / 12h.\n\nDead-letter queue \342\200\224 abandoned pipeline jobs are detected and quarantined.\n\nHealth checks \342\200\224 /live (process only), /health + /api/health (dependency health, 503 only on DB failure), /ready (strict: migrations, scheduler, feeds, notification backlog).\n\nMulti-worker safe \342\200\224 configurable SCHEDULER_OWNER, GUNICORN_WORKERS, SCHEDULER_REPLICA_COUNT with fail-closed validation.\n\nIdempotent pipeline \342\200\224 run_pipeline() is a pure function; re-runs with the same data never create duplicate tracking records.\n\nInfrastructure\nContainerized \342\200\224 Docker Compose with one-shot migration service before app startup\nDatabase \342\200\224 PostgreSQL (production) or SQLite (dev), Alembic-style schema migrations\nWSGI \342\200\224 Gunicorn with configurable workers/threads\nNTP \342\200\224 optional in-process sync with allowed-server whitelist\nBackups \342\200\224 custom-format PostgreSQL dumps with selective restore support\nEmail \342\200\224 Mailgun delivery disabled by default; graceful degradation when disabled"
    user_requests: "React + NextUI UI, remove SLA. this application is used for tracking products vulnerbilities and sending notification with no human intervention. UI should be professional not wih flashy colors."
    user_requests: "suggest imporvements"
    user_requests: "suggest improvements in matching and other core areas. sould be enterprise grade"
    user_requests: "implement all"
    user_requests: "move menu to left side panel with svg icons. clean UI. light mode and dark mode support. remove HTML Email Template box. show allow changes directly on Rendered Client Preview with options to change font color, font style, add drawing objects, change background color render live. rename Rendered Client Preview to HTML template. this template should apply to all new notifications. cve is matched by published date and also last modified date. add paginations where needed. make UI clean and neat. dashboard to have clickable cards."
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
    total_subagent_count: 0
  }
}
